ºxéÂ<–è'ºF:æªè!ºÓZÒ∫F:><à_N<W0~<öÉãº_Ω§k <%sï∫m,Ω¸’£ºúp␀ºà<˜ Z=fÚ|ºÆu*º®ÆÀª*rV=≤qâº›ÕÚºﬁs=„+ê∫¯ŸƒªS»<\∆˝<≥ñ‡<J®ºGΩ»¬<I¡SΩ˛¬òºZÂêºPDHºÏ¿–∫ùË´<≠π<çŸ<çÆÅº{"title": "VITAMINA B\u2082:Vitamin B\u2082, or riboflavin, acts as a cofactor in Red-Ox reactions and is found in dairy products and green vegetables."}{"title": "VITAMINA B\u2083:Vitamin B\u2083, also known as niacin, is an essential vitamin that plays a crucial role in various bodily functions. It is found in organ meats and several other foods. Additionally, niacin is utilized therapeutically to address deficiencies in the body."}{"title": "XEROFTALMIA:Xerophthalmia is a condition caused by vitamin A deficiency, leading to dryness of the cornea and potential blindness."}{"title": "DEGENERACI\u00d3N MACULAR:Age-related macular degeneration is an eye condition that can be influenced by vitamin deficiencies, particularly vitamin A."}{"title": "HEMORRAGIAS:Hemorragias refer to bleeding that can occur within adrenal masses, which may be discovered incidentally during medical examinations. Additionally, hemorrhages can arise from a significant deficiency of vitamin K, a crucial nutrient necessary for proper blood clotting. This highlights the importance of both anatomical factors, such as adrenal masses, and nutritional deficiencies in the occurrence of hemorragias."}{"title": "NEURITIS:Neuritis is an inflammation of the nerves that can be treated with vitamin B\u2081, highlighting its therapeutic utility."}{"title": "POLINEURITIS:Polyneuritis is a condition that can be treated with vitamin B\u2081, which is important for nerve health."}{"title": "BAJO NIVEL SOCIOECON\u00d3MICO:Low socioeconomic status can lead to nutritional deficiencies, including vitamin B\u2081, particularly in older adults."}{"title": "TIROTOXICOSIS:Thyrotoxicosis is a clinical syndrome characterized by elevated levels of thyroid hormones in the body, which can arise from various causes. This condition is not only significant for its hormonal implications but can also be associated with vitamin B\u2081 deficiency, which may impact neurological health."}{"title": "AYUNO PROLONGADO:Prolonged fasting can result in deficiencies of vitamins, particularly vitamin K."}{"title": "RECOMENDACIONES DIARIAS:Daily recommendations for vitamins A, K, B\u2081, B\u2082, and B\u2083 are essential for maintaining health."}{"title": "VITAMINA B\u2085:El \u00e1cido pantot\u00e9nico, conocido como vitamina B\u2085, es importante en la s\u00edntesis de \u00e1cidos grasos y se encuentra en abundancia en alimentos como carnes y legumbres."}{"title": "VITAMINA B\u2081\u2082:VITAMINA B\u2081\u2082, also known as cobalamina, is an essential nutrient that plays a vital role in the formation of red blood cells. It is primarily found in animal-based products. This vitamin is particularly important for older adults, as it is necessary for preventing anemia and maintaining cardiovascular health."}{"title": "LEGUMINOSAS:Las leguminosas son una fuente de nutrientes que incluyen varias vitaminas B, especialmente B\u2085 y B\u2086."}{"title": "LEVADURAS:Las levaduras son utilizadas en la producci\u00f3n de alimentos y son ricas en vitaminas del grupo B, incluyendo B\u2083 y B\u2086."}{"title": "HARINAS:Las harinas, especialmente las integrales, contienen vitaminas del grupo B, incluyendo B\u2083 y B\u2086."}{"title": "PAN INTEGRAL:PAN INTEGRAL, or whole grain bread, is recognized for its nutritional benefits, making it a healthier choice compared to white bread. It serves as a source of various B vitamins, including B\u2083 and B\u2086, and is notably higher in fiber content. Additionally, PAN INTEGRAL provides 2.5 mg of iron per 100 grams, contributing to its overall nutritional profile. It is also included in dietary recommendations for meals, emphasizing its role in a balanced diet."}{"title": "H\u00cdGADO DE BUEY:"}{"title": "GASTRITIS CR\u00d3NICA ATR\u00d3FICA:Gastritis cr\u00f3nica atr\u00f3fica is a chronic condition that can lead to decreased absorption of Vitamin B\u2081\u2082."}{"title": "GASTRECTOMIZADAS:Gastrectomizadas refers to individuals who have undergone gastrectomy, affecting their Vitamin B\u2081\u2082 absorption."}{"title": "COLISTIRAMINA:Colestiramina is a medication that can interfere with the absorption of Vitamin B\u2081\u2082. It is recommended that Colestiramina be taken with meals to help decrease gastrointestinal discomfort."}{"title": "PROTECTORES G\u00c1STRICOS:Protectores g\u00e1stricos, such as omeprazol, are medications that may reduce Vitamin B\u2081\u2082 absorption when used long-term."}{"title": "RIESGO CARDIOVASCULAR:Riesgo cardiovascular, or cardiovascular risk, encompasses the likelihood of developing heart-related conditions and is influenced by various factors, including lifestyle and dietary choices. It is a significant concern in the context of hormone replacement therapy, where its potential effects on heart health are closely monitored. Additionally, cardiovascular risk is a critical area of study in relation to diabetes, which is part of Samuel Namara's research focus. \n\nThe risk can also be heightened in patients with EPOC (chronic obstructive pulmonary disease) and is associated with Vitamin B\u2081\u2082 deficiency. Furthermore, the long-term health risks linked to the use of certain medications, such as fentermina, have been noted by the European Medicines Agency (EMA). Overall, understanding and managing cardiovascular risk is essential for preventing heart-related health issues."}{"title": "DISFUNCIONES NEUROL\u00d3GICAS:Disfunciones neurol\u00f3gicas are neurological disorders that can arise from Vitamin B\u2081\u2082 deficiency."}{"title": "SENSIBILIDAD PROFUNDA:Sensibilidad profunda refers to deep sensitivity issues that can occur due to Vitamin B\u2081\u2082 deficiency.)<|COMPLETE|>"}{"title": "CANCER DE PR\u00d3STATA:"}{"title": "ANIMO TRISTE:"}{"title": "INTOLERANCIA HIDROCARBONADA:"}{"title": "HORMONAS TIROIDEAS:HORMONAS TIROIDEAS, or thyroid hormones, are hormones produced by the thyroid gland, primarily including T3 (triiodothyronine) and T4 (thyroxine). These hormones are essential for regulating various metabolic processes in the body, including lipid metabolism and overall metabolic function. The production of thyroid hormones is dependent on the availability of iodine, and their synthesis can be affected by factors such as iodine deficiency.\n\nThyroid hormones are regulated by thyroid-stimulating hormone (TSH) and play a crucial role not only in metabolism but also in influencing sodium levels and fluid and electrolyte balance within the body. They are vital for normal development and function, and their levels are often assessed in the initial evaluation of patients, particularly those with eating disorders, to understand their metabolic status.\n\nAdditionally, thyroid hormones are involved in conditions such as hyperthyroidism, highlighting their significance in both health and disease. Overall, HORMONAS TIROIDEAS are critical for maintaining metabolic homeostasis and overall physiological balance."}{"title": "CANCER DE COLON:Colon cancer, also known as cancer de colon, is a medical condition that can be detected through specific dietary modifications and tests. This disease has been associated with various nutritional factors, including a notable link to selenium deficiency."}{"title": "PATOLOG\u00cdAS CARDIOVASCULARES:Cardiovascular diseases have been associated with selenium deficiency."}{"title": "METABOLISMO DE LA GLUCOSA:Glucose metabolism is influenced by chromium, which enhances insulin action."}{"title": "METABOLISMO LIP\u00cdDICO:Lipid metabolism is affected by chromium, which can lower total cholesterol and triglycerides."}{"title": "SAL YODADA:SAL YODADA refers to iodized salt, which serves as a common dietary source of iodine, an essential trace element necessary for maintaining proper health. It is widely utilized to meet the iodine requirements in the diet, ensuring that individuals receive adequate intake of this vital nutrient."}{"title": "BICIO:El bocio es una condici\u00f3n que se produce por la inflamaci\u00f3n de la gl\u00e1ndula tiroides, a menudo relacionada con la deficiencia de yodo."}{"title": "DEFICIENCIA DE ZINC:La deficiencia de zinc puede causar problemas de cicatrizaci\u00f3n, alteraciones neuropsicol\u00f3gicas y un sistema inmune debilitado."}{"title": "DEFICIENCIA DE COBRE:La deficiencia de cobre puede llevar a anemia, osteoporosis y alteraciones neurol\u00f3gicas."}{"title": "BORO:Boro refers to boron, a mineral that is recognized for its various roles in biological systems. While it is not classified as an essential trace element for humans, it is acknowledged in dietary guidelines with recommended daily intake levels. Boro is particularly important for animals and plants, contributing to cellular membrane stability and calcium metabolism."}{"title": "ACIDO FOLICO:Acido F\u00f3lico, also known as folic acid, is a B vitamin produced by intestinal bacteria and plays a crucial role in DNA synthesis and repair. It is essential for cell division and overall health, with a recommended daily intake of 200-400 \u03bcg for adults. Additionally, Acido F\u00f3lico is important for brain health, as it has been linked to cognitive function and the prevention of cognitive decline. In certain medical situations, such as hyper-homocysteinemia in patients undergoing dialysis, higher doses of 1-5 mg per day may be recommended. Folic acid levels are also measured in blood tests to assess a patient's health status."}{"title": "ENVEJECIMIENTO Y NUTRICION:Envejecimiento y Nutricion refers to the study of dietary needs and nutrition for the elderly population, focusing on trace elements and vitamins."}{"title": "INTERMOUNTAIN HEART COLLABORATIVE:The Intermountain Heart Collaborative (IHC) is a research group dedicated to studying cardiovascular health, with a particular emphasis on the effects of vitamin D deficiency on cardiovascular risk factors and disease status. This collaborative effort investigates various cardiovascular risk factors and the overall disease status within healthcare populations, aiming to enhance understanding and improve outcomes related to cardiovascular health."}{"title": "BIBLIOGRAFIA RECOMENDADA:Bibliograf\u00eda recomendada refers to the recommended literature for further reading on nutrition and health, particularly for the elderly."}{"title": "HELICOBACTER PYLORI:Helicobacter pylori is a type of bacteria that resides in the human stomach and is associated with various gastrointestinal diseases. It can cause infections that lead to conditions such as gastritis and peptic ulcer disease. Additionally, Helicobacter pylori is linked to atrophic gastritis, which may contribute to vitamin B12 deficiency. The presence of this bacterium can also result in iron deficiency due to malabsorption. Overall, Helicobacter pylori plays a significant role in gastrointestinal health and disease."}{"title": "GASTRECTOMIZED:Gastrectomized refers to individuals who have undergone surgical removal of part or all of the stomach, which can affect nutrient absorption, including iron."}{"title": "AMERICAN JOURNAL OF CARDIOLOGY:The American Journal of Cardiology is a peer-reviewed medical journal that publishes research related to cardiovascular health."}{"title": "COCHRANE DATABASE OF SYSTEMATIC REVIEWS:The Cochrane Database of Systematic Reviews is a comprehensive collection of high-quality systematic reviews that play a crucial role in informing healthcare decision-making. This database includes various studies, such as those focused on vitamin D supplementation, providing valuable insights and evidence to guide healthcare professionals and policymakers."}{"title": "BRITISH MEDICAL JOURNAL:The British Medical Journal (BMJ) is a leading peer-reviewed medical journal that publishes a wide range of research articles, reviews, and clinical guidelines in the field of medicine. It covers various medical topics, including but not limited to calcium and vitamin D supplementation, contributing to the advancement of medical knowledge and practice."}{"title": "EU PLATFORM FOR ACTION ON DIET, PHYSICAL ACTIVITY AND HEALTH:The EU Platform for Action on Diet, Physical Activity and Health is an initiative aimed at promoting healthy diets and physical activity across Europe."}{"title": "DAVID SMITH A:David Smith A is a researcher who has contributed to studies on the effects of folic acid and its benefits for health."}{"title": "YOUNG-IN K:Young-in K is a researcher involved in studies related to nutrition and health, particularly focusing on folic acid."}{"title": "FELDMAN EB:Feldman EB is an author recognized for his contributions to the field of nutrition, particularly focusing on older adults. He has written extensively on this topic, including a significant contribution to the Handbook of Nutrition and Food, where he addresses the nutritional needs and considerations for individuals in later years."}{"title": "NUTRITION IN THE LATER YEARS:Nutrition in the Later Years is a topic discussed in literature focusing on dietary needs and health in older adults."}{"title": "MYOCARDIAL INFARCTION:Myocardial infarction, commonly known as a heart attack, is a critical health event characterized by the blockage of blood flow to the heart, resulting in a medical emergency. This serious condition is influenced by various risk factors, including dietary intake. Research has shown that factors such as vitamin D and calcium intake, as well as omega-3 fatty acids, can play a significant role in the risk of experiencing a myocardial infarction. Understanding these dietary impacts is essential for managing and potentially reducing the risk of this life-threatening event."}{"title": "NONVERTEBRAL FRACTURES:Nonvertebral fractures are injuries that occur outside the vertebral column and have been studied in relation to vitamin D supplementation."}{"title": "AMINO ACID SUPPLEMENTATION:Amino acid supplementation is a dietary intervention studied for its effects on muscle mass and function, particularly in older adults."}{"title": "PLANT STEROL-ENRICHED SPREAD:Plant sterol-enriched spread is a dietary product studied for its cholesterol-lowering potential."}{"title": "EUROPEAN COMMISSION:The European Commission is the executive branch of the European Union responsible for proposing legislation and implementing decisions, including those related to health and nutrition."}{"title": "BRUSSELS:Brussels is the capital city of Belgium and the de facto capital of the European Union, where many health and nutrition policies are discussed."}{"title": "CALCIUM SUPPLEMENTS:"}{"title": "BERDANIER CD:Berdanier CD is the editor of the Handbook of Nutrition and Food, which includes contributions on nutrition for older adults."}{"title": "SOCIETY ESPA\u00d1OLA DE GERIATR\u00cdA Y GERONTOLOG\u00cdA:The Spanish Society of Geriatrics and Gerontology focuses on the health and nutrition of older adults."}{"title": "IM&C:IM&C is a publishing house that has published works related to nutrition and health for the elderly."}{"title": "NUTRITIONAL RECOMMENDATIONS:NUTRITIONAL RECOMMENDATIONS are comprehensive guidelines designed to enhance overall health and well-being through informed dietary choices. These recommendations focus on improving cardiovascular health by advising individuals to limit added sugars and sodium intake. They are particularly aimed at older adults, helping to improve their dietary habits and nutritional intake. Additionally, these guidelines are based on evidence and are intended to prevent and treat obesity and overweight conditions. Developed by various organizations, NUTRITIONAL RECOMMENDATIONS promote health and aim to prevent diseases through a balanced and mindful approach to diet."}{"title": "NUTRITION CLINICAL DIET HOSP:Nutritional Clinical Diet Hospital is a publication that discusses dietary recommendations for geriatric patients."}{"title": "NUTR RES:Nutrition Research is a journal that publishes studies related to nutrition, including vitamin D deficiency."}{"title": "N ENGL J MED:The New England Journal of Medicine (N Engl J Med) is a prestigious peer-reviewed medical journal that publishes a wide range of research articles, reviews, and case reports across various medical disciplines. Established as a leading source of medical knowledge, it has published significant studies on topics such as urinary sodium and potassium excretion and their relationship to cardiovascular events, as well as the causes, pathogenesis, and treatment of non-alcoholic steatohepatitis. The journal also focuses on the impacts of diet on health, including research related to obesity and its treatments, and cardiovascular health. Overall, N Engl J Med serves as a vital resource for medical professionals and researchers seeking comprehensive insights into contemporary medical issues."}{"title": "MART\u00cdNEZ \u00c1LVAREZ JR:Mart\u00ednez \u00c1lvarez JR is an author who has written about nutrition for educators."}{"title": "MOSS C:Moss C is an author who has researched gastrointestinal hormones and their effects on appetite in aging."}{"title": "MU\u00d1OZ C:Mu\u00f1oz C is an author who has contributed to the understanding of nutrition in healthy older adults."}{"title": "ONAMB\u00c9L\u00c9-PEARSON GL:Onamb\u00e9l\u00e9-Pearson GL is an author who has studied the effects of supplementation on exercise adaptations in older persons."}{"title": "RAMOS CORDERO P:Ramos Cordero P is an author known for his contributions to the field of nutrition, particularly focusing on healthy eating practices for the elderly. He has collaborated on various works that address the importance of nutrition and feeding in residential settings for older adults. Through his writings, Ramos Cordero P emphasizes the significance of proper dietary habits to enhance the well-being of the elderly population."}{"title": "HENDERSON GC:Henderson GC is an author who has researched the application of essential amino acid supplementation in treating sarcopenia in elderly people."}{"title": "HOLICK MF:Holick MF is an author known for his work on vitamin D deficiency and its implications for health."}{"title": "LIPS P:Lips P is an author who has contributed to research on reducing fracture risk with calcium and vitamin D."}{"title": "JACKSON RD:Jackson RD is an author who has studied the effects of calcium and vitamin D supplementation on fracture risk."}{"title": "LAVIE CJ:Lavie CJ is an author who has researched the role of omega-3 polyunsaturated fatty acids in cardiovascular diseases."}{"title": "LEE JH:Lee JH is an author who has discussed vitamin D deficiency as a cardiovascular risk factor."}{"title": "GIL GREGORIO P:"}{"title": "STEWART CE:Stewart CE is an author who has researched the influences of carbohydrate and amino acid supplementation on exercise adaptations in older individuals."}{"title": "ORTEGA RM:Ortega RM is an author recognized for their contributions to the field of nutrition, particularly in relation to dietary records and assessments. They have focused on the nutritional needs of the elderly, providing insights and recommendations for dietary intakes tailored to this specific population."}{"title": "REQUEJO AM:Requejo AM is an author who contributed to the recommendations of energy and nutrient intakes for the Spanish population."}{"title": "NAVIA B:Navia B is an author involved in establishing dietary recommendations for the Spanish population."}{"title": "L\u00d3PEZ-SOBALER AM:L\u00f3pez-Sobaler AM is an author who has worked on dietary recommendations and nutritional assessments."}{"title": "ORTIZ LEYBA C:Ortiz Leyba C is an author who has researched macronutrient and micronutrient requirements."}{"title": "PASIAKOS SM:Pasiakos SM is an author who has studied the effects of dietary leucine on muscle response to amino acids."}{"title": "PI\u00d1EIRO CORRALES G:Pi\u00f1eiro Corrales G is an author who has researched the role of omega-3 fatty acids in preventing cardiovascular diseases."}{"title": "REYNOLDS EH:Reynolds EH is an author who has discussed the benefits and risks of folic acid to the nervous system."}{"title": "RODR\u00cdGUEZ I:Rodr\u00edguez I is an author recognized for his contributions to the field of nutrition, specifically in the formulation and preparation of parenteral nutrition. Additionally, he has played a significant role in developing dietary intake recommendations aimed at promoting healthy consumption. Through his work, Rodr\u00edguez I has made important strides in both clinical nutrition and public health guidance."}{"title": "SHAPES SA:Shapses SA is an author who has reviewed the evidence on vitamin D and its role in preventing cardiovascular disease."}{"title": "SKARUPSKY KA:Skarupsky KA is an author who has studied the association of vitamins with depressive symptoms in older adults."}{"title": "SMITH GI:Smith GI is an author who has conducted research on the effects of omega-3 fatty acid supplementation on muscle protein synthesis in older adults."}{"title": "VEGA PI\u00d1ERO B:Vega Pi\u00f1ero B is an author who has written about nutritional requirements and aging."}{"title": "VIZUETE ARANZAZU A:Vizuete Aranzazu A is an author who has researched dietary factors related to depression in the elderly."}{"title": "WANG L:Wang L is an author who has conducted a systematic review on vitamin D and calcium supplementation for cardiovascular event prevention."}{"title": "ZOLTICK ES:Zoltick ES is an author who has studied the relationship between dietary protein intake and falls in older adults."}{"title": "FORMACI\u00d3N CONTINUADA DE NUTRICI\u00d3N Y OBESIDAD:Formaci\u00f3n continuada de Nutrici\u00f3n y Obesidad is a publication that discusses nutritional needs for the elderly."}{"title": "LA COMPOSICI\u00d3N DE LOS ALIMENTOS:La composici\u00f3n de los alimentos is a book that serves as a basic tool for nutritional assessment."}{"title": "AM J CLIN NUTR:The American Journal of Clinical Nutrition (Am J Clin Nutr) is a peer-reviewed journal dedicated to the field of clinical nutrition and its significant impact on health. It publishes a wide range of research articles that explore various aspects of nutrition, including its relationship with cancer risk, dietary practices, and overall health outcomes. Notably, the journal has featured systematic reviews and meta-analyses on topics such as the effects of fruit and vegetable intake on weight loss, as well as studies on dietary omega-3 fatty acid supplementation and its influence on muscle protein synthesis. Through its comprehensive coverage of clinical nutrition and dietetics, Am J Clin Nutr serves as a vital resource for researchers and practitioners interested in the implications of nutrition on health."}{"title": "NUTR CLIN DIET HOSP:Nutr Clin Diet Hosp is a journal that focuses on clinical nutrition and dietary practices in hospital settings."}{"title": "LIBRO BLANCO DE LA ALIMENTACI\u00d3N DE LOS MAYORES:Libro Blanco de la Alimentaci\u00f3n de los mayores is a publication that provides dietary recommendations for older adults."}{"title": "NUTR REV:Nutr Rev is a journal that reviews nutritional science, including studies on dietary leucine and muscle response."}{"title": "ED. COMPLUTENSE:Ed. Complutense is a publishing house that published works related to nutrition and dietary recommendations."}{"title": "M\u00c9DICA PANAMERICANA:M\u00e9dica Panamericana is a publishing house that published the Libro Blanco de la Alimentaci\u00f3n de los mayores.)<|COMPLETE|>"}{"title": "COLLABORATION:"}{"title": "WHITE BACKGROUND:The white background serves as a canvas for the text and logo, enhancing visibility and clarity of the design."}{"title": "DARK BLUE LETTERS:The word \"vegenat\" is presented in dark blue letters, which is part of the branding for the company."}{"title": "REGISTERED TRADEMARK SYMBOL:The registered trademark symbol (\u00ae) indicates that \"vegenat\" is a legally protected brand name."}{"title": "CIRCULAR GREEN ICON:"}{"title": "SAEDYN:SAEDYN, or the Sociedad Andaluza de Endocrinolog\u00eda, Diabetes y Nutrici\u00f3n, is a scientific society dedicated to the fields of endocrinology, diabetes, and nutrition in Andalusia. The organization plays a significant role in promoting these disciplines within the region and is involved in the accreditation of continuous training activities related to endocrinology and nutrition. Through its efforts, SAEDYN aims to enhance the knowledge and skills of professionals in these vital areas of health."}{"title": "ESTEVE PHARMACEUTICALS:Esteve Pharmaceuticals is a pharmaceutical company involved in the publication of clinical practice guidelines in endocrinology and nutrition."}{"title": "PAPENDOCRINIC:PapEndoCrinic is a clinical practice self-training program focused on endocrinology and nutrition."}{"title": "TIROIDES:The \"TIROIDES,\" or thyroid gland, is an essential endocrine gland located in the neck that plays a critical role in regulating metabolism, growth, and development. It produces several hormones, including thyroid hormones such as T3 (triiodothyronine) and T4 (thyroxine), as well as calcitonin, which is involved in calcium metabolism. The gland captures iodine, which is necessary for the synthesis of these hormones.\n\nThe thyroid is also significant in the context of various medical conditions. Its dysfunction can lead to disorders such as hypothyroidism and hyperthyroidism, which are characterized by an underactive or overactive thyroid, respectively. Additionally, the thyroid gland can be the site of serious health issues, including the development of medullary carcinomas and other forms of thyroid cancer.\n\nIn the field of endocrinology, the TIROIDES is a focal point for diagnostic studies and treatments, particularly concerning the differential diagnosis of conditions like TSH-producing pituitary tumors and thyroid hormone resistance. Overall, the thyroid gland is vital for maintaining metabolic balance and overall health in the human body."}{"title": "C\u00c1NCER DIFERENCIADO DE TIROIDES:C\u00e1ncer diferenciado de tiroides is a type of thyroid cancer that is addressed in clinical practice guidelines. This form of cancer is characterized by its ability to concentrate iodine in a manner similar to healthy thyroid tissue, which necessitates specific diagnostic follow-up. C\u00e1ncer diferenciado de tiroides generally includes papillary and follicular thyroid cancers and is associated with a better prognosis compared to other types of thyroid cancer."}{"title": "C\u00c1NCER MEDULAR DE TIROIDES:C\u00e1ncer medular de tiroides is another form of thyroid cancer discussed in the context of endocrinology."}{"title": "HIP\u00d3FISIS:The \"HIP\u00d3FISIS,\" also known as the pituitary gland, is a small but crucial endocrine gland located at the base of the brain. It plays a vital role in regulating various hormonal functions in the human body, including the production of hormones such as growth hormone (GH), prolactin, adrenocorticotropic hormone (ACTH), and thyroid-stimulating hormone (TSH). The gland is often referred to as the \"master gland\" due to its significant influence on other endocrine glands and its involvement in processes such as growth, metabolism, and fluid balance through the secretion of antidiuretic hormone (ADH).\n\nThe pituitary gland is divided into two main parts: the adenohypophysis (anterior pituitary) and the neurohypophysis (posterior pituitary). It can be affected by various conditions, including hyperplasia during pregnancy and hypothyroidism, as well as by tumors such as pituitary adenomas and metastases from other cancers, like breast and lung tumors. Additionally, there are instances where the pituitary gland may be involved in autoimmune conditions, such as suspected autoimmune hypophysitis in patients with a history of autoimmune diseases.\n\nThe development of the pituitary gland's hormonal secretion control system begins during gestation, highlighting its importance in endocrine functions from early life. Furthermore, the gland may also be impacted by conditions like iron overload in hemochromatosis, which can affect its normal functioning. Overall, the HIP\u00d3FISIS is essential for maintaining hormonal balance and regulating numerous physiological processes in the body."}{"title": "M\u00d3DULO 4:M\u00f3dulo 4 is dedicated to the topic of Nutrition and encompasses a comprehensive exploration of various aspects related to this field. It includes a series of questions and answers that address nutritional assessment and requirements, as well as enteral and parenteral nutrition. Additionally, M\u00f3dulo 4 covers special situations, eating disorders, and clinical cases, providing a well-rounded understanding of nutrition in different contexts."}{"title": "M\u00d3DULO 5:M\u00f3dulo 5 is a comprehensive educational module that covers a range of topics related to the adrenal glands. It includes detailed discussions on adrenal insufficiency, Cushing's syndrome, hyperaldosteronism, pheochromocytoma, incidentaloma, and adrenal carcinoma. Additionally, M\u00f3dulo 5 features a series of questions and answers that further explore the subject of adrenal health, providing a thorough understanding of the various conditions and functions associated with the adrenal glands."}{"title": "NUTRICI\u00d3N EN SITUACIONES ESPECIALES:Nutritional strategies tailored for specific medical conditions or circumstances."}{"title": "MISCELEANEA:The entity \"MISCELEANEA\" encompasses a diverse range of subjects. It includes a variety of substances that can induce the Syndrome of Inappropriate Antidiuretic Hormone secretion (SIADH), such as opiates and other medications. Additionally, \"MISCELEANEA\" covers various miscellaneous topics related to nutrition that do not fit into other specific categories. This broad scope highlights the entity's multifaceted nature, addressing both pharmacological aspects and nutritional themes."}{"title": "CASOS CL\u00cdNICOS:\"CASOS CL\u00cdNICOS\" refers to clinical case studies that serve to illustrate specific medical and nutritional conditions and their management. These case studies provide detailed examples that highlight various medical issues as well as nutritional challenges and treatments. They are utilized to enhance understanding of both medical and nutritional practices through specific clinical examples."}{"title": "INSUFICIENCIA SUPRARRENAL:\"INSUFICIENCIA SUPRARRENAL\" is a medical condition characterized by the inadequate production of hormones by the adrenal glands, specifically steroid hormones such as cortisol and aldosterone. This insufficiency affects the body's fluid and electrolyte balance and can lead to various health issues, including symptoms like hypoglycemia and fatigue. In summary, \"INSUFICIENCIA SUPRARRENAL\" occurs when the adrenal glands fail to produce sufficient amounts of essential hormones, resulting in significant physiological consequences."}{"title": "S\u00cdNDROME DE CUSHING:Cushing's syndrome, known as \"s\u00edndrome de Cushing\" in Spanish, is a hormonal disorder characterized by prolonged exposure to high levels of cortisol, a glucocorticoid hormone. This condition can arise from various causes, including tumors and the administration of medications. It is associated with specific clinical features and can manifest in different forms, either dependent or independent of adrenocorticotropic hormone (ACTH). \n\nIn particular, Cushing's syndrome can occur in approximately 30% of cases related to micronodular adrenal disease, which is linked to the Carney complex. Symptoms of the syndrome may include hirsutism, among other manifestations. Overall, Cushing's syndrome represents a significant medical condition that necessitates careful diagnosis and treatment due to its complex nature and the various underlying causes that can lead to excessive cortisol production."}{"title": "HIPERALDOSTERONISMO:Hyperaldosteronism, also known as Hiperaldosteronismo, is a medical condition characterized by the excessive production of the hormone aldosterone. This condition is often associated with adrenal incidentalomas, which are unexpected findings of adrenal tumors during imaging studies. Hyperaldosteronism is primarily related to excessive sodium retention in the body, leading to various health complications. The condition is discussed in detail in the Manual de Endocrinolog\u00eda y Nutrici\u00f3n, highlighting its significance in endocrinology and nutrition."}{"title": "FEOCROMOCITOMA:FEOCROMOCITOMA, also known as pheochromocytoma, is a rare tumor that originates from chromaffin cells in the adrenal glands. This tumor is characterized by the excessive production of catecholamines, which can lead to various clinical symptoms, including hypertension and hypertensive crises. It is often diagnosed through biochemical profiling and is important to rule out before surgical procedures, such as those for medullary thyroid carcinoma.\n\nPatients with FEOCROMOCITOMA may experience a range of symptoms due to the overproduction of catecholamines, and the condition is associated with certain genetic syndromes, including Cowden syndrome. Screening for this tumor is recommended starting at the age of 11 for individuals at risk. Treatment typically involves surgical intervention, which is necessary after proper medical preparation to manage the symptoms and potential complications, such as hypercalcemia due to excess PTHrP secretion.\n\nOverall, FEOCROMOCITOMA requires specific diagnostic and therapeutic approaches due to its potential malignancy and the serious health implications associated with its symptoms."}{"title": "INCIDENTALOMA SUPRARRENAL:The \"INCIDENTALOMA SUPRARRENAL\" refers to an adrenal incidentaloma, which is a mass found in the adrenal gland that is typically benign and non-functioning. These masses are often discovered incidentally during imaging studies conducted for unrelated medical conditions. Upon discovery, further evaluation may be necessary to assess the hormonal activity of the mass and to rule out the possibility of malignancy. The term \"incidentaloma suprarrenal\" specifically denotes an adrenal mass that requires careful assessment to determine its functionality and whether surgical removal (ex\u00e9resis) is needed."}{"title": "CARCINOMA SUPRARRENAL:Carcinoma suprarrenal is a rare primary malignant tumor that originates in the adrenal glands, with an incidence of approximately 1 in 1,000,000 inhabitants per year. This type of cancer is more commonly diagnosed in women and typically occurs in individuals between the ages of 40 to 50. Carcinoma suprarrenal may be suspected in cases of adrenal incidentalomas, which are unexpected findings of adrenal masses during imaging studies. Overall, carcinoma suprarrenal represents a significant concern in the context of adrenal cancer, highlighting the need for awareness and careful evaluation of adrenal masses."}{"title": "HIPERPLASIA SUPRARRENAL CONG\u00c9NITA:Hiperplasia suprarrenal cong\u00e9nita, also known as congenital adrenal hyperplasia, is a genetic disorder that significantly impacts the production of hormones in the adrenal glands. This condition is primarily caused by a deficiency of the enzyme 21-hydroxylase, which leads to an overproduction of androgens. As a result, individuals with this disorder may experience symptoms such as hirsutism and other hormonal imbalances. The disorder affects adrenal gland function, resulting in various health implications related to adrenal hormone production."}{"title": "S\u00cdNDROME POLIGLANDULAR AUTOINMUNE:S\u00cdNDROME POLIGLANDULAR AUTOINMUNE, also known as autoimmune polyglandular syndrome, is a medical condition characterized by the presence of multiple autoimmune disorders that affect the endocrine system. This syndrome may involve the association of two or more endocrine disorders mediated by an immune mechanism, which can include conditions such as diabetes mellitus and Addison's disease. Specifically, autoimmune polyglandular syndrome type 1 is noted for the destruction of the parathyroid glands, resulting in hypoparathyroidism and related complications. Additionally, this syndrome may be connected to other endocrine disorders discussed in the context of POEMS syndrome."}{"title": "METABOLISMO FOSFOC\u00c1LCICO:Metabolismo fosfoc\u00e1lcico refers to the metabolic processes involving calcium and phosphate in the body, crucial for bone health."}{"title": "TUMORES NEUROENDOCRINOS:TUMORES NEUROENDOCRINOS, or neuroendocrine tumors, are a group of neoplasias that can arise from neuroendocrine cells, which are responsible for hormone production and regulation. These tumors can occur in various parts of the body, including the digestive system, and may lead to symptoms such as chronic diarrhea. They are also associated with multiple endocrine neoplasia (MEN) syndromes, specifically MEN1 and MEN2. Research on neuroendocrine tumors is being conducted by Nuria Valdes Gallego, with a particular focus on paragangliomas and pheochromocytomas. Additionally, these tumors can have significant implications for hormone production, which may affect bone health and contribute to conditions like osteoporosis."}{"title": "MEN:MEN, or Multiple Endocrine Neoplasia, is a group of disorders that impact the endocrine glands, resulting in the formation of tumors and hormonal imbalances. Additionally, the term \"men\" refers to a demographic group that is often considered in dietary guidelines, which include specific nutritional recommendations tailored to their needs. This dual context highlights both the medical implications of MEN as a health condition and the nutritional considerations relevant to the male demographic."}{"title": "PUBERTAD PRECOZ:La pubertad precoz es un desarrollo sexual anormalmente temprano en ni\u00f1os, caracterizado por la aparici\u00f3n de caracter\u00edsticas sexuales secundarias antes de la edad normal, que se establece como antes de los 9 a\u00f1os para los ni\u00f1os y antes de los 7 a\u00f1os para las ni\u00f1as. Esta condici\u00f3n puede ser clasificada como central o perif\u00e9rica y puede estar asociada a diversas condiciones m\u00e9dicas. Aunque no es la causa m\u00e1s frecuente, la pubertad precoz puede manifestarse como un s\u00edntoma relacionado con tumores de la gl\u00e1ndula pineal. En resumen, la pubertad precoz es una manifestaci\u00f3n cl\u00ednica que conlleva importantes implicaciones m\u00e9dicas y requiere atenci\u00f3n adecuada."}{"title": "RETRASO PUBERAL:Retraso puberal is a condition characterized by delayed onset of puberty, which may require medical evaluation."}{"title": "HIPOGONADISMOS:Hipogonadismos refers to conditions where the body doesn't produce enough sex hormones, affecting sexual development and function."}{"title": "TRASTORNOS DE LA DIFERENCIACI\u00d3N SEXUAL:Trastornos de la diferenciaci\u00f3n sexual are conditions that affect the development of sexual characteristics, leading to atypical sexual development."}{"title": "HIRSUTISMO:Hirsutismo is a condition characterized by excessive or abnormal hair growth in women, particularly in areas where men typically grow hair. This condition is often associated with increased androgen levels, a phenomenon known as hyperandrogenism, and can arise from various underlying causes, including hormonal imbalances."}{"title": "TRANSEXUALES:Transexuales refers to individuals whose gender identity differs from the sex they were assigned at birth, often undergoing medical procedures for transition."}{"title": "OTROS:Otros refers to various other conditions or topics that may not fit into specific categories but are relevant in medical discussions."}{"title": "G\u00d3NADAS:G\u00d3NADAS are the organs responsible for producing gametes, which are the reproductive cells necessary for sexual reproduction. In humans, the gonads are represented by the testes in males and the ovaries in females. Additionally, in the context of hormone therapy, gonads may undergo surgical alteration or removal, impacting their function in gamete production."}{"title": "HIPERCALCEMIA:HIPERCALCEMIA is a medical condition characterized by abnormally high levels of calcium in the blood, typically defined as serum calcium levels exceeding 10.5 mg/dl. This condition is often associated with various medical issues, including hyperparathyroidism, which is a common cause, as well as malignancies such as certain tumors. The elevated calcium levels can lead to a range of health complications, potentially affecting kidney function and altering a patient's nutritional needs. Treatment is often required to lower calcium levels and manage the associated health risks. Hipercalcemia can occur in a small percentage of the population and is an important condition to consider in the context of parathyroid hormone and its implications for patient health."}{"title": "HIPOCALCEMIA:HIPOCALCEMIA is a medical condition characterized by low calcium levels in the blood, defined as a serum calcium level below 8.5 mg/dl. This condition can lead to various health issues, including muscle spasms and complications in patients with conditions such as pancreatitis. Hypocalcemia can also occur in patients receiving parenteral nutrition and is commonly observed in hospitalized patients."}{"title": "TRASTORNOS ELECTROLITICOS:Trastornos electrol\u00edticos refer to electrolyte disorders, which can disrupt the balance of electrolytes in the body, affecting various physiological functions."}{"title": "M\u00d3DULO 8:M\u00f3dulo 8 is a section in a medical text that discusses obesity, lipids, and electrolyte disorders, providing insights into these health issues."}{"title": "CASOS CLINICOS:"}{"title": "VIRGINIA BELLIDO CASTA\u00d1EDA:Dr. Virginia Bellido Casta\u00f1eda is a distinguished medical professional specializing in endocrinology and nutrition. She serves as the Head of Section at the Endocrinology and Nutrition Service of Hospital Universitario Cruces, located in Barakaldo, Vizcaya. In addition to her clinical responsibilities, Dr. Bellido Casta\u00f1eda focuses on nutritional labeling, contributing her expertise to the field of nutrition. Her affiliation with Hospital Universitario Cruces underscores her commitment to advancing healthcare in endocrinology and nutrition."}{"title": "DIEGO BELLIDO GUERRERO:Diego Bellido Guerrero is a Doctor in Medicine and a specialist in Endocrinology and Nutrition. He serves as the Head of Service at the Complex University Hospital of El Ferrol, also known as Complejo Hospitalario Universitario de Ferrol, located in A Coru\u00f1a, Spain. In his role, he is involved in diet therapy and nutrition, contributing to various topics related to healthy eating. He is affiliated with the University of A Coru\u00f1a and is recognized as a professional in the Endocrinology and Nutrition Service at the hospital."}{"title": "HOSPITAL UNIVERSITARIO CRUCES:Hospital Universitario Cruces is a medical facility located in Barakaldo, Vizcaya, near Bilbao. It specializes in endocrinology and nutrition. The hospital is notable for its leadership in the Endocrinology and Nutrition section, with Dr. Fco. Javier Santamar\u00eda Sandi serving as the Head of this section since 2007. Additionally, Virginia Bellido Casta\u00f1eda is also mentioned as working in the same department, holding the position of Head of Section in Endocrinology and Nutrition."}{"title": "COMPLEJO HOSPITALARIO UNIVERSITARIO DE EL FERROL:The Complex University Hospital of El Ferrol is a healthcare institution where Diego Bellido Guerrero serves as the Head of Service in Endocrinology and Nutrition."}{"title": "SOCIEDAD ANDALUZA DE ENDOCRINOLOG\u00cdA, DIABETES Y NUTRICI\u00d3N:The Sociedad Andaluza de Endocrinolog\u00eda, Diabetes y Nutrici\u00f3n (SAEDYN) is a scientific and professional society dedicated to the fields of endocrinology, diabetes, and nutrition. It plays a significant role in the accreditation of continuous training activities related to these specialties, ensuring that healthcare professionals remain updated with the latest knowledge and practices. The society is currently presided over by Mart\u00edn L\u00f3pez de la Torre Casares, who leads its initiatives and activities aimed at advancing the understanding and treatment of endocrine disorders and nutritional issues in the Andalusian region."}{"title": "LABORATORIOS ESTEVE:Laboratorios Esteve is a pharmaceutical company that sponsored the educational material for the project discussed in the document."}{"title": "ENDOCRINOLOGY AND NUTRITION:The specialty of Endocrinology and Nutrition encompasses the study and management of various pathologies related to hormonal and nutritional health."}{"title": "PRESENTACI\u00d3N:The presentation discusses the specialty of Endocrinology and Nutrition, highlighting the need for continuous education and the resources available for professionals in the field."}{"title": "DIABETES 2.0:Diabetes 2.0 is a working group within the Spanish Society of Diabetes (SED) focused on modern approaches to diabetes management."}{"title": "T\u00c9CNICAS APLICADAS A LA DIABETES:The Applied Technologies in Diabetes is a working group within the Spanish Society of Diabetes (SED) that focuses on technological advancements in diabetes care."}{"title": "DR. MART\u00cdN CUESTA HERN\u00c1NDEZ:Dr. Mart\u00edn Cuesta Hern\u00e1ndez is a specialist in Endocrinology and Nutrition at Hospital Universitario Cl\u00ednico San Carlos in Madrid."}{"title": "DR. MIGUEL A. RUBIO HERRERA:Dr. Miguel A. Rubio Herrera is the Head of the Endocrinology and Nutrition Section at Hospital Cl\u00ednico San Carlos in Madrid."}{"title": "DR. FRANCISCO JAVIER ESCALADA SAN MART\u00cdN:Dr. Francisco Javier Escalada San Mart\u00edn is the Director of the Department of Endocrinology and Nutrition at Cl\u00ednica Universidad de Navarra in Pamplona."}{"title": "DR. FCO. JAVIER SANTAMAR\u00cdA SANDI:Dr. Fco. Javier Santamar\u00eda Sandi is the Head of the Endocrinology Section at Hospital Universitario Cruces in Barakaldo, Vizcaya."}{"title": "DR. MART\u00cdN L\u00d3PEZ DE LA TORRE CASA:Dr. Mart\u00edn L\u00f3pez de la Torre Casares is the Head of the Endocrinology and Nutrition Service at Hospital Universitario Virgen de las Nieves in Granada."}{"title": "DRA. ANA M.\u00aa URIOSTE FONDO:Dra. Ana M.\u00aa Urioste Fondo works in the Endocrinology and Nutrition Service at Complejo Asistencial Universitario de Le\u00f3n."}{"title": "DR. \u00d3SCAR MORENO P\u00c9REZ:Dr. \u00d3scar Moreno P\u00e9rez is the Coordinator of the Diabetes Unit in the Endocrinology and Nutrition Service at Hospital General Universitario de Alicante."}{"title": "DRA. NURIA VALD\u00c9S GALLEGO:Dra. Nuria Vald\u00e9s Gallego works in the Endocrinology and Nutrition Service at Hospital Universitario Central de Asturias in Oviedo."}{"title": "DR. PEDRO JOS\u00c9 PIN\u00c9S CORRALES:Dr. Pedro Jos\u00e9 Pin\u00e9s Corrales works in the Endocrinology and Nutrition Service at Complejo Hospitalario Universitario de Albacete."}{"title": "DR. ALFONSO VIDAL CASARIEGO:Dr. Alfonso Vidal Casariego works in the Endocrinology and Nutrition Service at Complexo Hospitalario Universitario de A Coru\u00f1a."}{"title": "DRA. REBECA REYES GARC\u00cdA:Dra. Rebeca Reyes Garc\u00eda works in the Endocrinology and Nutrition Service at Hospital Universitario Torrec\u00e1rdenas in Almer\u00eda."}{"title": "DRA. ROC\u00cdO VILLAR TAIBO:Dra. Roc\u00edo Villar Taibo is a specialist in Endocrinology and Nutrition at Complejo Hospitalario Universitario de Santiago de Compostela in A Coru\u00f1a."}{"title": "HOSPITAL CL\u00cdNICO SAN CARLOS:Hospital Cl\u00ednico San Carlos is a prominent medical facility located in Madrid, Spain. It offers a wide range of healthcare services, with a particular emphasis on endocrinology, nutrition, and geriatrics. The hospital is staffed by several physicians, including Dr. Miguel A. Rubio Herrera, who serves as the Head of the Endocrinology and Nutrition Section. Dr. Rubio Herrera specializes in clinical nutrition and obesity, contributing to the hospital's focus on these critical areas of healthcare. Additionally, Mart\u00edn Cuesta Hern\u00e1ndez is another endocrinologist working at the hospital, further enhancing its expertise in endocrinology. Overall, Hospital Cl\u00ednico San Carlos is recognized for its comprehensive medical services and specialized care in various fields."}{"title": "CL\u00cdNICA UNIVERSIDAD DE NAVARRA:Cl\u00ednica Universidad de Navarra is a prominent medical institution located in Pamplona, Spain. It is known for its specialized departments, including the Department of Endocrinology and Nutrition, which is directed by Dr. Francisco Javier Escalada San Mart\u00edn. Dr. Escalada San Mart\u00edn has been associated with the clinic, contributing his expertise to the field of endocrinology and nutrition."}{"title": "HOSPITAL UNIVERSITARIO VIRGEN DE LAS NIEVES:Hospital Universitario Virgen de las Nieves is a medical facility located in Granada, Spain. It is recognized as a healthcare institution where Dr. Mart\u00edn L\u00f3pez de la Torre Casares holds the position of Head of the Endocrinology and Nutrition Service."}{"title": "COMPLEJO ASISTENCIAL UNIVERSITARIO DE LE\u00d3N:The Complejo Asistencial Universitario de Le\u00f3n is a healthcare institution dedicated to the treatment and research of obesity and related conditions. It serves as a medical facility where Dra. Ana M.\u00aa Urioste Fondo is employed in the Endocrinology and Nutrition Service, contributing to the institution's focus on addressing health issues associated with obesity."}{"title": "HOSPITAL UNIVERSITARIO CENTRAL DE ASTURIAS:The Hospital Universitario Central de Asturias is a prominent medical facility located in Oviedo, Asturias, Spain. It specializes in various fields, with a particular focus on endocrinology and nutrition. The hospital is home to several specialists, including Dra. Nuria Vald\u00e9s Gallego and Dr. Francisco Villaz\u00f3n Gonz\u00e1lez, who work within the Endocrinology and Nutrition Service. This institution is recognized for its comprehensive healthcare services and expertise in managing endocrine disorders and nutritional issues."}{"title": "COMPLEJO HOSPITALARIO UNIVERSITARIO DE ALBACETE:The Complejo Hospitalario Universitario de Albacete, also known as the University Hospital Complex of Albacete, is a prominent medical facility that provides a range of healthcare services. Within this institution, Dr. Pedro Jos\u00e9 Pin\u00e9s Corrales serves as a specialist in the Endocrinology and Nutrition Service, contributing his expertise to the treatment and management of endocrine disorders and nutritional health."}{"title": "COMPLEXO HOSPITALARIO UNIVERSITARIO DE A CORU\u00d1A:The Complexo Hospitalario Universitario de A Coru\u00f1a is a comprehensive medical facility that offers a range of healthcare services. Within this institution, Dr. Alfonso Vidal Casariego is a notable professional working in the Endocrinology and Nutrition Service. The hospital is dedicated to providing assistance and care to patients, supported by a team of skilled medical professionals."}{"title": "HOSPITAL UNIVERSITARIO TORREC\u00c1RDENAS:Hospital Universitario Torrec\u00e1rdenas is a medical facility located in Almer\u00eda, Spain. It is notable for its Endocrinology and Nutrition Service, where Dra. Rebeca Reyes Garc\u00eda serves as an attending physician."}{"title": "COMPLEJO HOSPITALARIO UNIVERSITARIO DE SANTIAGO DE COMPOSTELA:Complejo Hospitalario Universitario de Santiago de Compostela is a medical facility where Dra. Roc\u00edo Villar Taibo works in the Endocrinology and Nutrition Service."}{"title": "HOSPITAL UNIVERSITARIO CL\u00cdNICO SAN CARLOS:"}{"title": "ADENOHIP\u00d3FISIS:The adenohip\u00f3fisis, also known as the anterior pituitary, is the front part of the pituitary gland responsible for the production of several hormones. Among these hormones are prolactin and gonadotropins, which play crucial roles in various physiological processes within the body."}{"title": "NEUROHIP\u00d3FISIS:The neurohip\u00f3fisis, or neurohypophysis, is the posterior part of the pituitary gland. It plays a crucial role in the endocrine system by storing and releasing hormones that are produced in the hypothalamus. Among the key hormones released by the neurohip\u00f3fisis are oxytocin and vasopressin, also known as antidiuretic hormone (ADH). These hormones are essential for various physiological functions, including regulating water balance and facilitating childbirth."}{"title": "BOLSA DE RATHKE:La bolsa de Rathke es una estructura embrionaria que da origen a la adenohip\u00f3fisis durante el desarrollo fetal."}{"title": "HIPOTALAMO:El hipot\u00e1lamo es una regi\u00f3n del cerebro que regula la secreci\u00f3n de hormonas hipofisarias a trav\u00e9s de hormonas adenohipofisotropas."}{"title": "PROLACTINA:Prolactina es una hormona producida por la adenohip\u00f3fisis, que desempe\u00f1a un papel crucial en la regulaci\u00f3n de la lactancia. Su producci\u00f3n est\u00e1 bajo el control inhibidor de la dopamina, lo que significa que la dopamina act\u00faa para limitar la secreci\u00f3n de prolactina en el organismo."}{"title": "TSH:TSH, or Thyroid-Stimulating Hormone, is a crucial hormone produced by the adenohypophysis (anterior pituitary gland) that plays a significant role in regulating thyroid function. It stimulates the thyroid gland to produce thyroid hormones, which are essential for metabolism, growth, and overall bodily functions. TSH levels are often measured in blood tests to evaluate thyroid function and can indicate various health conditions.\n\nIn patients with conditions such as hypophysitis, TSH may be deficient, leading to alterations in thyroid hormone synthesis. Additionally, low TSH levels can be observed in individuals with Anorexia Nerviosa, reflecting changes in the thyroid axis due to malnutrition. The regulation of TSH itself is influenced by Thyrotropin-Releasing Hormone (TRH), and its release follows a circadian pattern.\n\nTSH is also significant in the context of diagnosing and treating hypothyroidism, particularly in patients with pituitary deficiencies. It serves as a threshold for confirmatory studies in congenital hypothyroidism and is monitored in patients with thyroid disorders to assess their thyroid function. Overall, TSH is vital for maintaining normal thyroid activity and metabolic health."}{"title": "GH:GH, or Growth Hormone, is a crucial hormone that plays a significant role in growth, metabolism, and body composition in humans and other animals. Its secretion is episodic and regulated by various physiological factors, exhibiting a diurnal rhythm. GH stimulates growth, cell reproduction, and regeneration, making it essential for development and overall health. In the context of patient diagnosis and treatment, GH deficiency is a critical concern, as it can impact growth and metabolic functions. Additionally, while GH is sometimes considered for nutritional support, there is insufficient evidence to support its effectiveness in this area. In certain cases, such as hypophysitis, GH levels may remain normal despite deficiencies in other hormones. Overall, GH is vital for maintaining proper physiological functions related to growth and metabolism."}{"title": "FSH:FSH, or Follicle-Stimulating Hormone, is a crucial gonadotropin produced by the adenohypophysis (anterior pituitary gland) that plays a significant role in regulating reproductive processes. It is essential for the development of eggs in the ovaries of females and the production of sperm in the testes of males. FSH is involved in the regulation of the menstrual cycle and is also relevant in diagnosing conditions such as pubertal delays and endocrine function through hormonal studies.\n\nIn addition to its primary functions, FSH can be present at normal levels in certain medical conditions, such as hypophysitis, which distinguishes it from other hormones like ACTH and TSH. The hormone stimulates the growth of ovarian follicles in women and activates Sertoli cells in the testes to facilitate sperm production. Overall, FSH is vital for sexual development and reproductive health in both genders."}{"title": "LH:LH, or luteinizing hormone, is a crucial gonadotropin that plays a significant role in the regulation of the menstrual cycle and ovulation in females. It is responsible for triggering ovulation and stimulating the production of testosterone in males by acting on the Leydig cells in the testes. LH can be present at normal levels in cases of hypophysitis, which distinguishes it from other hormones such as ACTH and TSH. In summary, LH is essential for reproductive health, influencing both female ovulation and male testosterone production, and is often measured in hormonal studies to assess hormonal balance."}{"title": "FACTORES SOLUBLES DE CRECIMIENTO:Los factores solubles de crecimiento son prote\u00ednas que pueden influir en la regulaci\u00f3n de la secreci\u00f3n de hormonas en la adenohip\u00f3fisis."}{"title": "RETROALIMENTACI\u00d3N NEGATIVA:La retroalimentaci\u00f3n negativa es un mecanismo de control que regula la secreci\u00f3n de hormonas hipofisarias a trav\u00e9s de hormonas perif\u00e9ricas segregadas en los \u00f3rganos diana."}{"title": "DOPAMINA:Dopamina, also known as dopamine, is a crucial neurotransmitter synthesized in the brain that plays a significant role in various physiological functions. It is involved in mood regulation, motor control, and the inhibition of prolactin secretion in the adenohypophysis. Additionally, dopamine is mentioned in the context of tesofensina's mechanism of action, highlighting its importance in pharmacological processes. Overall, dopamine serves as an essential regulator of hormonal activity and contributes to numerous neurological functions."}{"title": "OXITOCINA:OXITOCINA is a hormone produced in the hypothalamus and released by the neurohypophysis. It plays a crucial role in childbirth and lactation, facilitating these essential physiological processes. Additionally, oxytocin exhibits antidiuretic effects, contributing to various other physiological functions within the body."}{"title": "VASOPRESINA:VASOPRESINA, also known as antidiuretic hormone (ADH), is a hormone produced in the hypothalamus and released by the neurohypophysis. It plays a crucial role in regulating water retention in the kidneys, thereby helping to maintain the body's fluid balance. In addition to its primary function in water regulation, vasopresina is also implicated in the regulation of adrenocorticotropic hormone (ACTH) and has been studied in relation to thyroid function. Overall, vasopresina is essential for maintaining homeostasis in the body through its various regulatory roles."}{"title": "CITOCINAS:CITOCINAS son prote\u00ednas que desempe\u00f1an un papel crucial en la comunicaci\u00f3n celular. Estas mol\u00e9culas son fundamentales para influir en la inflamaci\u00f3n y la respuesta inmune del organismo."}{"title": "GHRH:GHRH, or growth hormone-releasing hormone, is a hormone that plays a crucial role in stimulating the release of growth hormone (GH) from the pituitary gland. Additionally, GHRH is involved in the regulation of luteinizing hormone (LH) and follicle-stimulating hormone (FSH). This hormone is essential for various physiological processes, including growth and metabolism, by promoting the secretion of growth hormone."}{"title": "SOMATOSTATINA:SOMATOSTATINA is a hormone produced by pancreatic delta cells that plays a crucial role in inhibiting the secretion of several other hormones, including growth hormone (GH), thyrotropin-releasing hormone (TRH), prolactin (PRL), and adrenocorticotropic hormone (ACTH) in the pituitary gland. This inhibitory function makes somatostatin significant in various medical treatments. \n\nSomatostatin is utilized in the treatment of pituitary tumors and is effective in managing complications following surgery, such as anastomotic dehiscence. Additionally, it is employed in the treatment of specific conditions like chylothorax and lymphatic fistulas, where it helps reduce gastrointestinal secretions and lymphatic flow. \n\nMoreover, somatostatin analogs are medications derived from this hormone that can be administered in parenteral nutrition under specific circumstances. These analogs are particularly useful in treating VIPoma, a type of tumor that secretes vasoactive intestinal peptide, by inhibiting its secretion. They are also used in managing acromegaly, a condition characterized by excessive growth hormone, and are often combined with dietary modifications to enhance treatment efficacy."}{"title": "ACTH:ACTH, or Adrenocorticotropic Hormone, is a hormone produced by the pituitary gland that plays a crucial role in stimulating the adrenal glands to release cortisol. This hormone is significant in the diagnosis and treatment of various conditions, particularly Cushing's disease and adrenal insufficiency. ACTH is involved in the regulation of cortisol production and can also influence the secretion of other hormones, such as aldosterone and ADH, under certain conditions.\n\nThe secretion of ACTH follows a circadian rhythm and is regulated by hypothalamic corticotropin-releasing hormone (CRH) and other factors. It is often measured in the evaluation of adrenal function and is essential for diagnosing conditions like congenital adrenal hyperplasia and pituitary disorders such as hypophysitis, which can lead to hormonal deficiencies.\n\nIn summary, ACTH is a vital hormone that not only stimulates cortisol production in the adrenal glands but also plays a key role in various diagnostic processes related to adrenal health and hormonal balance."}{"title": "CORTISOL:Cortisol is a steroid hormone produced by the adrenal glands, playing a crucial role in regulating metabolism, immune response, and the body's response to stress. It is essential for maintaining blood glucose levels and influencing sodium balance. Cortisol levels are critical in diagnosing and managing conditions such as Cushing's syndrome and adrenal insufficiency. In patients with adrenal insufficiency, cortisol metabolism is affected by the enzyme CYP3A4, which may necessitate dosage adjustments, particularly when drugs that inhibit CYP3A4 are involved.\n\nElevated cortisol levels can be observed in various conditions, including Anorexia Nervosa, and excessive cortisol can lead to a state resembling Cushing's syndrome, known as pseudo-Cushing. Additionally, cortisol can stimulate mineralocorticoid receptors and may affect insulin sensitivity during pregnancy. Overall, cortisol is a vital hormone that impacts numerous physiological processes, and its levels must be carefully monitored in clinical settings."}{"title": "IGF-1:IGF-1, or Insulin-like Growth Factor 1, is a crucial hormone that plays a significant role in growth and development throughout various life stages, including during pregnancy and childhood. It is structurally similar to insulin and is primarily influenced by growth hormone levels. IGF-1 is essential for promoting growth and development, exhibiting anabolic effects in adults, and is often monitored in clinical settings, particularly during growth hormone treatment and in evaluations of growth hormone deficiency.\n\nThe hormone's levels can be altered in individuals with eating disorders, such as Anorexia Nervosa, and its expression is also affected by nutritional status and glucocorticoids. Additionally, IGF-1 is important for bone health and development, and its measurement is utilized to assess the effectiveness of treatments for conditions like acromegaly, diabetes, and hypopituitarism. Notably, IGF-1 functions as a suppressor of growth hormone production, indicating a complex regulatory relationship between these two hormones. Overall, IGF-1 is a vital factor in understanding growth dynamics and metabolic health."}{"title": "CRH:CRH, or corticotropin-releasing hormone, is a hormone released by the hypothalamus that plays a crucial role in the body's stress response. It stimulates the release of adrenocorticotropic hormone (ACTH) from the pituitary gland, which is essential for regulating various physiological processes related to stress. Overall, CRH is integral to the endocrine system's response to stressors, facilitating the communication between the hypothalamus and the pituitary gland."}{"title": "IDINA:Idina is a standard test in pediatric endocrinology."}{"title": "CONE RD:CONE RD is an author known for contributions in the field of neuroendocrinology."}{"title": "LOW MJ:Low MJ is an author recognized for significant contributions to the field of neuroendocrinology. Their work is frequently referenced in the literature, highlighting their influence and expertise in this area of study."}{"title": "ELMQUIST JK:Elmquist JK is an author recognized for contributions to the field of neuroendocrinology. Their work is frequently cited in relevant studies, highlighting their significance in advancing understanding within this area of research."}{"title": "CAMERON JL:Cameron JL is an author recognized for significant contributions in the field of neuroendocrinology. He has been referenced in various contexts, particularly for his work that enhances the understanding of growth hormone functions. Additionally, Cameron JL has made notable contributions to the literature concerning the management of pancreatitis, further establishing his expertise in these areas of medical research."}{"title": "LARSEN PR:Larsen PR is a prominent author and editor in the field of endocrinology, particularly recognized for his contributions to thyroid physiology. He is known for his work in the endocrinology textbook referenced, and he serves as an editor of the \"Williams Textbook of Endocrinology.\" This comprehensive textbook covers various topics, including hormonal regulation, disorders, and specific conditions such as pheochromocytoma. Through his editorial role, Larsen PR has significantly influenced the understanding and dissemination of knowledge in endocrinology."}{"title": "KRONENBERG HM:Kronenberg HM is a prominent figure in the field of endocrinology, recognized as both a co-author and editor of the \"Williams Textbook of Endocrinology.\" His contributions to this comprehensive work encompass a wide range of topics within endocrinology, including hormonal influences on bone health, calcium metabolism, and parathyroid function. Additionally, he has provided insights into the treatment of hypercalcemia and the study of neuroendocrine tumors. As an editor, Kronenberg HM has played a significant role in advancing endocrine research and education, particularly in relation to conditions such as pheochromocytoma and insulinoma. His extensive involvement in the textbook underscores his expertise and commitment to the field of endocrinology."}{"title": "MELMED S:Melmed S is a prominent researcher and author in the field of endocrinology, particularly known for his contributions to the understanding and treatment of various endocrine disorders. He has made significant contributions to the literature on the adenohypophysis and the treatment of disorders related to prolactin. Melmed S is notably recognized for his work on acromegaly, having authored clinical practice guidelines for this condition.\n\nHe is one of the authors and editors of the \"Williams Textbook of Endocrinology,\" a comprehensive resource that covers a wide range of topics within endocrinology, including the treatment of osteoporosis and the management of neuroendocrine tumors. His contributions to this textbook have provided valuable insights into various endocrine disorders, including insulinoma and pheochromocytoma. Through his extensive work, Melmed S has established himself as a key figure in the field of endocrinology, influencing both clinical practice and academic research."}{"title": "POLONSKY KS:Polonsky KS is a prominent figure in the field of endocrinology, recognized for his significant contributions as both a co-author and editor of the \"Williams Textbook of Endocrinology.\" His work has greatly enhanced the understanding of various hormonal regulations and disorders, including conditions such as insulinoma, osteoporosis, hypercalcemia, and neuroendocrine tumors. As an editor, Polonsky KS has played a crucial role in shaping the content of the textbook, providing insights into endocrine functions and specific conditions like pheochromocytoma. His contributions have established him as a key authority in the field, making the \"Williams Textbook of Endocrinology\" a vital resource for understanding complex endocrine issues."}{"title": "TRH:TRH (Thyrotropin-Releasing Hormone) is a hypothalamic factor and a hormone that plays a crucial role in the endocrine system by stimulating the secretion of Thyroid-Stimulating Hormone (TSH) from the pituitary gland."}{"title": "HORMONAS DEL EJE HIPOT\u00c1LAMO-HIP\u00d3FISO-TIROIDEO:Hormones of the hypothalamic-pituitary-thyroid axis are involved in the regulation of thyroid function."}{"title": "SUE\u00d1O PROFUNDO:Deep sleep is mentioned as a physiological factor that stimulates the secretion of growth hormone."}{"title": "GNRH:Gonadotropin-Releasing Hormone (GnRH) is a vital hormone that plays a crucial role in the regulation of the reproductive system. It is responsible for stimulating the release of gonadotropins, specifically follicle-stimulating hormone (FSH) and luteinizing hormone (LH), from the pituitary gland. This release is essential for reproductive health and is involved in the onset of puberty. Additionally, GnRH is utilized in the treatment of conditions such as cryptorchidism, where it stimulates testosterone production. Overall, GnRH is integral to the functioning of the reproductive system and the regulation of sexual hormone production."}{"title": "IGFBP3:IGFBP3 is the main binding protein for IGF-1, abundant in plasma, and plays a crucial role in regulating the availability of IGF-1 in the body."}{"title": "ELSEVIER ESPA\u00d1A:Elsevier Espa\u00f1a is a publishing company that published the Spanish version of the 10th edition of the original work on endocrinology."}{"title": "WALTHAM:Waltham is a city located in Massachusetts, USA, and serves as the headquarters for UpToDate Inc. This organization is a valuable resource for medical professionals, providing updated medical information and guidelines on a variety of health conditions, including hyperaldosteronism, osteoporosis treatment, and insulinoma. UpToDate Inc. is recognized for its comprehensive medical information, making it an essential tool for healthcare providers seeking current and reliable data."}{"title": "UPTODATE INC.:UpToDate Inc. is a clinical decision support resource and medical information provider based in Waltham, MA. It is renowned for offering evidence-based information tailored for healthcare professionals across a wide range of medical topics. The organization provides comprehensive literature reviews and clinical guidelines that cover various conditions, including adrenal incidentalomas, congenital adrenal hyperplasia, Cushing's syndrome, insulinoma, hypoglycemia, vitamin D deficiency, osteoporosis treatment, and pheochromocytoma. UpToDate Inc. is dedicated to ensuring that healthcare professionals have access to the most current and relevant medical information to aid in the diagnosis and treatment of patients."}{"title": "SNYDER PJ:Snyder PJ is an author recognized for his contributions to the field of endocrinology, particularly in the areas of hyperprolactinemia and hypopituitarism. He has written extensively on the causes and management of hyperprolactinemia, detailing its clinical manifestations and implications. Additionally, Snyder PJ is referenced in the context of male hypogonadism, focusing on its clinical features and diagnosis. His work also encompasses research related to growth hormone, further establishing his expertise in endocrinological disorders."}{"title": "HYP\u00d3FISIS:The hypophysis, or pituitary gland, is a crucial gland in the endocrine system that regulates various hormones, including growth hormone."}{"title": "HESX1:HESX1 is a transcription factor associated with early activation cascades and linked to septo-optic dysplasia when mutated."}{"title": "LHX3:LHX3 is a transcription factor that, when mutated, can cause neurological anomalies due to its expression in the central nervous system."}{"title": "LHX4:LHX4 is a transcription factor involved in the early differentiation of pituitary cells."}{"title": "PROP-1:PROP-1 is a transcription factor that is the most common cause of combined pituitary deficits, leading to various hormonal deficiencies."}{"title": "PIT-1:PIT-1, also known as POU1F1, is a crucial transcription factor that plays a significant role in the differentiation of somatotropic, lactotropic, and, to a lesser extent, thyrotropic precursor cells. This protein is essential for the proper development and function of these hormone-producing cells in the pituitary gland."}{"title": "T-PIT:T-PIT is a transcription factor that is essential for the specific differentiation of corticotropic cells. It plays a crucial role in the development of pituitary cells and is involved in the regulation of growth hormone production."}{"title": "DISPLASIA SEPT\u00d3PTICA:Septo-optic dysplasia is a condition characterized by optic nerve hypoplasia, pituitary hormone alterations, and midline brain defects."}{"title": "HIPOPITUITARISMO:HIPOPITUITARISMO, or hypopituitarism, is a medical condition characterized by the insufficient production of one or more hormones by the pituitary gland. This condition can lead to a variety of health issues, including hormonal deficiencies and clinical symptoms such as amenorrhea primary. The pituitary gland may fail to produce adequate amounts of hormones, including growth hormone, which is crucial for various bodily functions. Hypopituitarism can manifest as either partial or total loss of pituitary hormonal function and is often discussed within the field of endocrinology, particularly concerning the treatment and monitoring of growth hormone levels. Additionally, it may require management in patients with pituitary tumors and can occur as an adverse effect of certain treatments, such as ipilimumab. Overall, hypopituitarism represents a significant clinical syndrome that necessitates careful evaluation and management."}{"title": "HORMONAS HIPOFISARIAS:Hormonas hipofisarias are hormones produced by the pituitary gland that play a vital role in regulating various endocrine functions within the body. These hormones are essential for numerous bodily processes, including growth, metabolism, and reproduction. They are particularly significant in the context of hormone replacement therapy, especially for individuals experiencing deficiencies due to conditions such as hypopituitarism. Hormonas hipofisarias include hormones like ACTH and prolactin, which can be influenced by various factors, including mutations in transcription factors and conditions such as hypophysitis. Overall, the proper functioning of these hormones is crucial for maintaining overall health and well-being."}{"title": "GEN\u00c9TICAS:GEN\u00c9TICAS refers to the genetic factors that play a significant role in various medical conditions. One of the primary etiologies of hypopituitarism, a condition characterized by hormonal deficiencies, is linked to genetic influences. Additionally, germline mutations in the prolactin receptor gene have been associated with hyperprolactinemia, a condition marked by elevated levels of prolactin in the blood. This highlights the importance of genetic factors in both hormonal regulation and related disorders."}{"title": "ADULTOS:\"ADULTOS\" refers to adults, who are individuals that have reached maturity and possess different nutritional requirements compared to children and infants. In the context of dietary guidelines for managing diabetes, adults are included as they generally tolerate starch and glucose polymers; however, they should avoid these if symptoms persist on a sucrose-free diet. Adults over the age of 19 are specifically referenced in energy requirement calculations. Additionally, adults can experience health issues such as adrenal insufficiency due to hypopituitarism and may face complications like osteomalacia or osteoporosis, particularly those with inflammatory bowel disease (EII), which can arise from malnutrition and other related factors. To maintain metabolic health, adults are advised to follow a balanced diet that includes corn starch and other essential nutrients. Furthermore, while adults may benefit from a ketogenic diet, its effectiveness may diminish over time due to low adherence to the dietary regimen."}{"title": "FERN\u00c1NDEZ-RODR\u00cdGUEZ E:Fern\u00e1ndez-Rodr\u00edguez E is an author recognized for significant contributions to the literature on hypopituitarism, particularly focusing on its diagnosis and treatment. Additionally, Fern\u00e1ndez-Rodr\u00edguez E has made important contributions to the study of hypothalamic-pituitary pathology, further enhancing the understanding of these related medical conditions."}{"title": "BERNABEU I:Bernabeu I is an author engaged in research on pituitary tumors and their pathology. Additionally, Bernabeu I has co-authored works that explore hypopituitarism, emphasizing its clinical implications and management strategies. Through these contributions, Bernabeu I has made significant strides in understanding and addressing conditions related to the pituitary gland."}{"title": "CASANUEVA FF:Casanueva FF is an author known for their contributions to the field of endocrinology, particularly in the study of prolactin disorders. They have authored a publication that discusses various aspects of these disorders, with a specific focus on the epidemiology and causes, while excluding prolactin-secreting pituitary tumors. In addition to their work on prolactin disorders, Casanueva FF has also researched hypopituitarism, exploring its treatment options. Furthermore, they have written extensively about pituitary tumors and their management, showcasing a comprehensive understanding of these related conditions within the endocrine system."}{"title": "MUTACIONES:MUTACIONES refers to genetic mutations that can have significant implications for various health conditions. Notably, mutations in the CYP21A2 gene are responsible for the majority of cases of congenital adrenal hyperplasia and can occur either de novo or be inherited. Additionally, mutations in the PTEN gene are crucial for the diagnosis and management of Cowden syndrome and other related neoplastic syndromes. These genetic alterations can also lead to conditions such as hypopituitarism, which affects hormone production and regulation. Furthermore, mutations can be associated with hereditary conditions, including feochromocitomas and paragangliomas. The PAH gene is another critical area, where over 400 mutations have been identified, leading to various forms of phenylketonuria. Specific mutations in the RTFQ gene have been documented, particularly within the Spanish population. Lastly, mutations in the X-ALD gene are responsible for adrenoleukodystrophy, a condition that impacts the metabolism of very long-chain fatty acids. Overall, the study of MUTACIONES encompasses a wide range of genetic changes that can lead to diverse and significant health issues."}{"title": "ADENOMAS HIPOFISARIOS:Adenomas hipofisarios are the most common type of pituitary tumors, characterized as benign growths that affect the pituitary gland. These tumors can lead to various hormonal imbalances and conditions, such as hypopituitarism, which is a deficiency in one or more of the hormones produced by the pituitary gland. Additionally, adenomas hipofisarios can cause hyperprolactinemia, a condition resulting from the overproduction of prolactin. Overall, these tumors can significantly impact hormonal function and health."}{"title": "HIPOFISITIS:Hipofisitis is an inflammatory condition of the pituitary gland, also known as the hypophysis. This inflammation can lead to various symptoms, including headaches and diabetes insipidus. Additionally, it may result in hypopituitarism, which is a deficiency in hormone production due to damage to the hormone-producing cells of the gland. The condition can be caused by infections or autoimmune processes. Characteristic findings of hipofisitis can be observed through magnetic resonance imaging (MRI)."}{"title": "S\u00cdNDROME DE SHEEHAN:S\u00edndrome de Sheehan is a condition that occurs due to pituitary gland damage during childbirth, leading to hypopituitarism."}{"title": "CRANEORAFINGIOMAS:Craneofaringiomas, also known as craniopharyngiomas, are tumors that can impact the pituitary gland, potentially resulting in hormonal deficiencies such as hypopituitarism. These tumors originate from remnants of Rathke's pouch and account for approximately 1-3% of all brain tumors. They exhibit a bimodal distribution, primarily affecting both children and adults."}{"title": "SARCOIDOSIS:Sarcoidosis is an inflammatory disease that can impact various organs, including the pituitary gland. This condition may lead to several complications, such as diabetes insipidus and hypopituitarism, both of which are related to the dysfunction of the pituitary gland. Additionally, sarcoidosis can cause hypercalcemia, which results from the increased endogenous production of calcitriol. Overall, sarcoidosis presents a range of potential health issues, particularly concerning endocrine function and calcium metabolism."}{"title": "HISTIOCITOSIS:Histiocitosis is a group of disorders that can involve the pituitary gland and result in hormonal deficiencies, including hypopituitarism."}{"title": "TALLA HIPOFISARIA:Talla hipofisaria refers to the development of the pituitary stalk, which can be affected in conditions leading to hypopituitarism."}{"title": "TUMORES HIPOFISARIOS:Los tumores hipofisarios son neoplasias que se desarrollan en la gl\u00e1ndula pituitaria y tienen la capacidad de secretar hormonas como la TSH (hormona estimulante de la tiroides) y la GH (hormona de crecimiento), entre otras."}{"title": "HORMONAS HIPOT\u00c1LAMO-HIPOFISARIAS:Hormones produced by the hypothalamus and pituitary gland that regulate various physiological processes."}{"title": "PRL:Prolactin (PRL) is a hormone produced by the pituitary gland that plays a crucial role in lactation, promoting milk production in mammals. In addition to its primary function in lactation, PRL is involved in the regulation of the menstrual cycle and has various roles in metabolism, immune system regulation, and the development of the reproductive system. Elevated levels of prolactin can occur in certain medical conditions, such as pituitary adenomas, particularly in patients with Multiple Endocrine Neoplasia type 1 (MEN1), and in individuals with acromegaly. Overall, PRL is essential for reproductive health and has significant implications in various physiological processes."}{"title": "COOPER DS:Cooper DS is an editor associated with the medical resource UpToDate, which provides comprehensive information on various medical conditions, including hyperprolactinemia and hypopituitarism. As an editor, Cooper DS has contributed to the publication, ensuring that it includes relevant and up-to-date information on these topics, thereby serving as a valuable resource in the field of medical literature."}{"title": "MARTIN KA:Martin KA is an editor who has made significant contributions to the medical resource UpToDate. His work includes providing information on hyperprolactinemia, a condition characterized by elevated levels of prolactin in the blood, as well as contributing to the understanding of hypopituitarism, a disorder resulting from insufficient hormone production by the pituitary gland. Martin KA is referenced in the context of medical literature related to both of these conditions, highlighting his role in enhancing the knowledge and resources available in the field of medicine."}{"title": "LOPEZ-FERNANDEZ J:L\u00f3pez-Fern\u00e1ndez J is an author known for contributing to the field of endocrinology through the creation of a manual that addresses hypopituitarism. Additionally, L\u00f3pez-Fern\u00e1ndez J is one of the authors of the \"Manual de Endocrinolog\u00eda y Nutrici\u00f3n,\" which offers valuable insights into both endocrinology and nutrition practices. This work reflects a comprehensive understanding of the interplay between hormonal health and nutritional factors."}{"title": "OLIVA GARC\u00cdA JG:Oliva Garc\u00eda JG is an author of a manual on endocrinology that discusses hypopituitarism."}{"title": "P\u00c9REZ LUIS JM:P\u00e9rez Luis JM is an author of a manual on endocrinology that discusses hypopituitarism."}{"title": "UPTODATE:UpToDate is a comprehensive online clinical decision support resource that offers evidence-based information for healthcare professionals across a wide range of medical topics. It provides up-to-date literature reviews, clinical guidelines, and detailed information on various conditions, including adrenal incidentalomas, primary aldosteronism, Cushing's syndrome, hyperparathyroidism, hypercalcemia, delayed puberty, primary adrenal insufficiency, hypopituitarism, pheochromocytoma, and acromegaly. \n\nThe platform is designed to assist healthcare providers by delivering current and relevant medical knowledge, including epidemiology, clinical manifestations, diagnosis, and treatment options for numerous conditions. UpToDate is recognized for its role in enhancing clinical decision-making and improving patient care through its extensive database of medical information. Additionally, it includes resources on dietary therapy and obesity in adults, further broadening its scope of support for healthcare professionals."}{"title": "MANUAL DE ENDOCRINOLOG\u00cdA Y NUTRICI\u00d3N:The \"Manual de Endocrinolog\u00eda y Nutrici\u00f3n\" is a comprehensive guide published by the Sociedad Espa\u00f1ola de Endocrinolog\u00eda y Nutrici\u00f3n. It serves as a valuable reference for various aspects of endocrinology and nutrition, including the treatment and management of endocrine disorders. The manual discusses lipid metabolism and provides dietary recommendations for managing lipid levels, specifically addressing dyslipidemias. It includes detailed information on the epidemiology, diagnosis, and classification of dyslipidemias, as well as treatment guidelines.\n\nAdditionally, the manual covers a range of endocrine disorders, such as Cushing's syndrome, primary adrenal insufficiency, congenital adrenal hyperplasia, and primary hyperaldosteronism. It also provides insights into hypopituitarism and includes guidelines on enteral and parenteral nutrition. Overall, the \"Manual de Endocrinolog\u00eda y Nutrici\u00f3n\" is an essential resource for healthcare professionals seeking to understand and manage various endocrine and nutritional issues effectively."}{"title": "TRITOS NA:Tritos NA is an editor of the book 'Prolactin disorders' which discusses various aspects of prolactin-related conditions."}{"title": "KLIBANSKY A:Klibansky A is an editor of the book 'Prolactin disorders' which covers the clinical management of prolactin disorders."}{"title": "SPRINGER NATURE SWITZERLAND AG:Springer Nature Switzerland AG is a publishing company that specializes in the publication of scientific works. Among its notable contributions is the book titled \"Prolactin disorders,\" which addresses various topics related to prolactin disorders. The company is recognized for its commitment to disseminating scholarly information in the field of science."}{"title": "HUMANA PRESS:Humana Press is a division of Springer Nature that focuses on publishing scientific and medical literature, including the book 'Prolactin disorders'."}{"title": "PROLACTIN DISORDERS:Prolactin disorders is a medical condition discussed in the book, focusing on the epidemiology, causes, and management of prolactin-related issues."}{"title": "DIABETES INS\u00cdPIDA:Diabetes ins\u00edpida is a medical condition characterized by excessive thirst (polydipsia) and the excretion of large amounts of severely diluted urine (polyuria), leading to an imbalance in body fluids. This disorder arises from the body's inability to concentrate urine, often due to dysfunctions in the hypothalamus or pituitary gland. It can be associated with neurogenic causes, such as necrosis of the neurohypophysis, and may also occur as a result of untreated adrenal insufficiency. In some cases, it is linked to the presence of pituitary adenomas or hypothalamic damage due to pineal tumors, which disrupt the regulation of water in the body. The condition is discussed in the context of treatment options, including glucocorticoid replacement therapy, as outlined in the Manual de Endocrinolog\u00eda y Nutrici\u00f3n."}{"title": "GLUCOCORTICOIDES:Glucocorticoides, or glucocorticoids, are a class of steroid hormones that play a significant role in regulating metabolism and the body's response to stress. They are commonly used in the treatment of various medical conditions, including adrenal insufficiency and adrenal disorders. These hormones can affect sex hormone-binding globulin (SHBG) levels and overall hormonal balance. \n\nIn clinical practice, glucocorticoids are utilized to manage conditions such as congenital adrenal hyperplasia, where they help control hormonal levels. Additionally, they can reduce aldosterone production in specific situations. However, the use of glucocorticoids is associated with certain risks, including an increased likelihood of fractures and the potential development of Cushing's syndrome due to their effects on the body.\n\nOverall, glucocorticoids are important medications in the management of various endocrine and metabolic disorders, but their administration requires careful consideration of dosage adjustments and monitoring for adverse effects."}{"title": "BANBURY:Banbury is a town in Oxfordshire, UK, where a community-based study on pituitary adenomas was conducted."}{"title": "SWEDEN:Sweden is a country known for its significant contributions to medical research, particularly in the fields of cardiovascular disease and bariatric surgery. It has been the site of various studies examining cardiovascular disease and mortality rates following bariatric surgery, including a nationwide observational cohort study that provided valuable insights into these health issues. Additionally, Sweden has conducted research on the incidence and prevalence of TSH-secreting pituitary adenomas, further highlighting its role in advancing medical knowledge. Furthermore, Sweden is one of the five northern European countries that played a crucial role in the establishment of the Enhanced Recovery After Surgery (ERAS) group, which focuses on improving surgical recovery protocols."}{"title": "CUSHING'S SYNDROME:Cushing's syndrome is a hormonal disorder characterized by excessive levels of cortisol in the body, often resulting from prolonged exposure to this hormone. The condition can arise due to various causes, including pituitary adenomas, which are tumors in the pituitary gland that produce adrenocorticotropic hormone (ACTH), leading to increased cortisol production. Symptoms of Cushing's syndrome may include weight gain, skin changes, muscle weakness, elevated cortisol levels in urine, and disordered gonadal function. The disorder is associated with various endocrine disorders and can lead to significant health issues if left untreated.\n\nDiagnosis of Cushing's syndrome requires specific methods to confirm the presence of high cortisol levels and to identify the underlying cause. Treatment options typically involve medications that inhibit steroidogenesis or cortisol synthesis, aiming to reduce cortisol levels and alleviate symptoms. Overall, Cushing's syndrome necessitates a comprehensive approach to diagnosis and management due to its complex nature and the range of clinical manifestations it presents."}{"title": "HYPOTHALAMUS:The hypothalamus is a critical region of the brain that plays a vital role in controlling the pituitary gland and regulating various hormonal functions within the body. It is integral to the endocrine system, influencing the secretion of adrenocorticotropic hormone (ACTH) from the pituitary gland. Additionally, the hypothalamus is involved in the dysregulation that can lead to hypogonadotropic hypogonadism, particularly in patients suffering from Anorexia Nervosa. This highlights its importance not only in general hormone regulation but also in specific medical conditions related to hormonal imbalances."}{"title": "HYPOTHALAMIC-PITUITARY AXIS:The hypothalamic-pituitary axis is a complex and critical regulatory system in the body that encompasses a set of interactions between the hypothalamus and the pituitary gland. This axis plays a vital role in regulating numerous bodily functions by influencing the function of the pituitary gland and the hormones it produces."}{"title": "CORTICOTROPINOMA:Corticotropinoma is a type of pituitary adenoma that produces ACTH and can lead to Cushing's syndrome."}{"title": "MACROADENOMA:MACROADENOMA refers to a type of pituitary adenoma that is characterized by its size, measuring larger than 1 cm. This condition is more prevalent in women and can lead to various symptoms due to the tumor's size and location. One of the significant effects of a macroadenoma is the production of excess prolactin, which can result in hyperprolactinemia. Additionally, macroadenomas are commonly associated with Multiple Endocrine Neoplasia type 1 (MEN1). The presence of a macroadenoma can also lead to hypogonadotropic hypogonadism, further complicating the clinical picture. Overall, macroadenomas are notable for their potential to cause a range of hormonal and physical symptoms due to their impact on the pituitary gland."}{"title": "HYPOTHYROIDISM:Hypothyroidism is a common endocrine disorder characterized by the insufficient production of thyroid hormones by the thyroid gland. This condition can be associated with various factors, including Klinefelter syndrome, which is a genetic condition that can lead to hormonal imbalances. Additionally, hypothyroidism can be induced by the medication amiodarone, which affects thyroid function and may result in decreased hormone production. The condition can also be related to pituitary function, indicating that issues with the pituitary gland may contribute to the development of hypothyroidism. Overall, hypothyroidism is a multifaceted disorder that can arise from genetic, medication-related, and endocrine system factors."}{"title": "HYPOPITUITARISM:Hypopituitarism is a medical condition characterized by the insufficient production of certain hormones by the pituitary gland. This condition can arise in various contexts, including in patients with hereditary hemochromatosis, a genetic disorder that can lead to decreased hormone production from the pituitary gland."}{"title": "PROLACTINOMAS:Prolactinomas are a specific type of pituitary adenoma characterized by the overproduction of prolactin, a hormone that can lead to a range of health complications. These tumors are particularly prevalent among patients with Multiple Endocrine Neoplasia type 1 (MEN1), a genetic condition that affects the endocrine glands. The excess prolactin produced by prolactinomas can result in various symptoms and health issues, making them significant in the context of endocrine disorders."}{"title": "FERNANDEZ A:Fernandez A is an author referenced in a study on the prevalence of pituitary adenomas."}{"title": "KARAVITAKI N:Karavitaki N is an author referenced in a study on the prevalence of pituitary adenomas."}{"title": "WASS J:Wass J is an author referenced in a study on the prevalence of pituitary adenomas."}{"title": "OXFORDSHIRE:Oxfordshire is a county in England where Banbury is located, relevant to the study of pituitary adenomas."}{"title": "CORTICOTROPINOMAS:Corticotropinomas are a type of pituitary tumor that can lead to various hormonal imbalances and require careful monitoring post-surgery."}{"title": "ADENOMAS:Adenomas are non-functioning tumors that primarily occur in the pituitary gland, necessitating close observation due to the potential for complications. Additionally, adenomas can also develop in the liver, particularly in patients with hepatic glycogenosis type I, where there is a risk that these tumors may become malignant."}{"title": "DIABETES INSIPIDA:Diabetes insipida is a medical condition characterized by excessive thirst and urination, which is often associated with issues related to the pituitary gland. This condition can lead to severe dehydration and hypernatremia, particularly affecting vulnerable populations such as infants and elderly patients with cognitive impairment."}{"title": "ENFERMEDAD DE CUSHING:The \"ENFERMEDAD DE CUSHING,\" also known as Cushing's disease, is an endocrine disorder characterized by elevated levels of cortisol in the body. This condition can arise from various causes, most commonly due to pituitary tumors, specifically corticotropinomas, which produce excess adrenocorticotropic hormone (ACTH). The elevated cortisol levels can lead to secondary hypertension and potassium loss, highlighting the importance of dietary management in affected individuals. Treatment for Cushing's disease may be necessary to control the symptoms and manage the hormonal imbalance effectively."}{"title": "TUMORES PINEALES:TUMORES PINEALES, or pineal tumors, are rare tumors that can affect the pineal gland. These tumors are classified into several types, including germ cell tumors and others."}{"title": "HISTIOCITOSIS X:Histiocytosis X is a rare disease characterized by the proliferation of histiocytes, which can affect various organs including the pituitary gland."}{"title": "ENFERMEDAD DE ERDHEIM-CHESTER:Erdheim-Chester disease is a rare form of non-Langerhans histiocytosis that can cause systemic symptoms and affect the pituitary gland."}{"title": "GLANDULA PINEAL:The pineal gland is a small endocrine gland in the brain that produces melatonin and can be affected by tumors."}{"title": "LOPES MB:Lopes MB is an author who co-wrote the overview of the 2017 WHO Classification of Pituitary Tumors."}{"title": "AND\u00daJAR P:And\u00fajar P is an author who wrote about the pathology of the hypothalamic-pituitary axis and pineal tumors."}{"title": "JACOBSEN E:Jacobsen E is an author who has written about Erdheim-Chester disease."}{"title": "METE O:"}{"title": "GL\u00c1NDULA PINEAL:La gl\u00e1ndula pineal es una peque\u00f1a gl\u00e1ndula endocrina en el cerebro que produce melatonina y est\u00e1 relacionada con varios tumores, como los germinomas."}{"title": "GERMINOMAS:Los germinomas son un tipo de tumor que se origina en las c\u00e9lulas germinales y son los m\u00e1s frecuentes en la gl\u00e1ndula pineal."}{"title": "S\u00cdNDROME DE PARINAUD:El s\u00edndrome de Parinaud es un conjunto de s\u00edntomas neurol\u00f3gicos que puede presentarse en pacientes con tumores en la regi\u00f3n pineal, as\u00ed como en aquellos con tumores en la regi\u00f3n selar, como los adenomas hipofisarios. Uno de los s\u00edntomas caracter\u00edsticos del s\u00edndrome de Parinaud es la par\u00e1lisis de la mirada superior, que puede afectar la capacidad del paciente para mover los ojos hacia arriba. Este s\u00edndrome es relevante en el contexto de tumores que afectan estas \u00e1reas del cerebro, indicando la necesidad de una evaluaci\u00f3n neurol\u00f3gica en pacientes con tales condiciones."}{"title": "HCG:Human Chorionic Gonadotropin (HCG) is a hormone produced during pregnancy that plays a crucial role in stimulating thyroid hormone production and influencing TSH (Thyroid Stimulating Hormone) levels. In addition to its role in pregnancy, HCG is utilized in medical treatments to stimulate testosterone production in males. It is important to note that HCG can also be produced by tumors of the pineal gland, which may lead to effects on the production of both testosterone and estrogens. Furthermore, HCG can cause secondary hyperthyroidism by binding to the TSH receptor. Overall, HCG is a multifaceted hormone with significant implications in both reproductive health and endocrine function."}{"title": "AIP:AIP is a tumor suppressor gene that plays a significant role in the development of pituitary adenomas. It is particularly associated with isolated familial pituitary adenomas (FIPA). Additionally, the AIP gene may also be linked to the formation of craniopharyngiomas."}{"title": "MEN1:MEN1, or Multiple Endocrine Neoplasia Type 1, is a hereditary genetic syndrome that significantly increases the risk of developing multiple endocrine tumors. This condition is characterized by the formation of tumors in various endocrine glands, including the parathyroid glands, anterior pituitary, and pancreatic islet cells. Among the tumors associated with MEN1 are gastrinomas, which produce the gastrin hormone, and insulinomas, which are linked to a prevalence of 6-10% in cases of insulinoma. MEN1 is recognized as a tumor suppressor gene and is a focus of clinical guidelines and treatment strategies aimed at managing the associated risks of both endocrine and non-endocrine tumors. Overall, MEN1 is a complex syndrome that necessitates careful monitoring and management due to its multifaceted impact on endocrine health."}{"title": "PRKARIA:PRKARIA es un gen que act\u00faa como supresor tumoral y est\u00e1 implicado en la patogenia de los adenomas hipofisarios."}{"title": "RB:RB es un gen supresor tumoral que se ha asociado con la aparici\u00f3n de adenomas hipofisarios."}{"title": "GNAS:GNAS is a gene that encodes the alpha subunit of the stimulatory G protein, playing a crucial role in the regulation of hormone signaling pathways, particularly those associated with growth hormone. This gene can be mutated in pituitary adenomas, which are tumors that can affect hormone production. GNAS is recognized as an oncogene and is particularly implicated in the formation of pituitary adenomas, especially somatotroph adenomas, which are characterized by excessive growth hormone secretion."}{"title": "H-RAS:H-RAS es un oncog\u00e9n que se ha implicado en la aparici\u00f3n de adenomas hipofisarios."}{"title": "CCND1:CCND1 es un oncog\u00e9n relacionado con la proliferaci\u00f3n celular y se ha implicado en adenomas hipofisarios."}{"title": "HMGA2:HMGA2 es un oncog\u00e9n que se ha asociado con la formaci\u00f3n de adenomas hipofisarios."}{"title": "FGFR4:FGFR4 es un oncog\u00e9n que puede estar implicado en la aparici\u00f3n de adenomas hipofisarios."}{"title": "GADD45G:GADD45G es un inhibidor de la proliferaci\u00f3n que se ha relacionado con adenomas hipofisarios."}{"title": "MEG3:MEG3 es otro inhibidor de la proliferaci\u00f3n implicado en la patogenia de los adenomas hipofisarios."}{"title": "CDKN1B:CDKN1B is a gene that encodes a cyclin-dependent kinase inhibitor, which has been associated with the development of pituitary adenomas. Additionally, CDKN1B may be studied in the context of Multiple Endocrine Neoplasia type 1 (MEN1) syndrome, especially in cases where mutations in the MEN1 gene are not identified."}{"title": "CCNB2:CCNB2 es una ciclina que se ha implicado en la proliferaci\u00f3n celular y en adenomas hipofisarios."}{"title": "PPTG:PPTG es una prote\u00edna que se ha relacionado con la regulaci\u00f3n del ciclo celular y adenomas hipofisarios."}{"title": "LIQUIDO CEFALORRAQU\u00cdDEO:El l\u00edquido cefalorraqu\u00eddeo es un fluido que puede verse afectado por tumores pineales, provocando un aumento de oncoprote\u00ednas."}{"title": "ONCOPROTE\u00cdNAS:Las oncoprote\u00ednas son prote\u00ednas que pueden ser producidas por tumores, como los germinomas, y est\u00e1n relacionadas con el l\u00edquido cefalorraqu\u00eddeo."}{"title": "ALTERACIONES VISUALES:Las alteraciones visuales son un s\u00edntoma neurol\u00f3gico que puede aparecer en pacientes con tumores de la gl\u00e1ndula pineal."}{"title": "CEFALEA:La cefalea es un s\u00edntoma com\u00fan que aparece en el 73% de los casos de tumores pineales."}{"title": "NAUSEAS Y V\u00d3MITOS:Las n\u00e1useas y v\u00f3mitos son s\u00edntomas que pueden presentarse en pacientes con tumores de la gl\u00e1ndula pineal, afectando su calidad de vida."}{"title": "ALTERACIONES EN LA DEAMBULACI\u00d3N:Las alteraciones en la deambulaci\u00f3n son un s\u00edntoma que puede aparecer en pacientes con tumores de la gl\u00e1ndula pineal, afectando su movilidad."}{"title": "AFECTACI\u00d3N SUPRASELAR:La afectaci\u00f3n supraselar se refiere a la invasi\u00f3n de estructuras por tumores, lo que puede causar endocrinopat\u00edas en pacientes."}{"title": "RITMO CIRCADIANO:El ritmo circadiano puede verse alterado en pacientes con tumores de la gl\u00e1ndula pineal, afectando su sue\u00f1o y estado de alerta."}{"title": "HIDROCEFALIA:La hidrocefalia es una condici\u00f3n que puede resultar de la obstrucci\u00f3n del flujo del l\u00edquido cefalorraqu\u00eddeo debido a tumores pineales."}{"title": "ALTERACIONES EN LA REGULACI\u00d3N DEL APETITO:Las alteraciones en la regulaci\u00f3n del apetito pueden ser consecuencia de la afectaci\u00f3n hipotal\u00e1mica por tumores de la gl\u00e1ndula pineal."}{"title": "MELATONINA:La melatonina es una hormona producida por la gl\u00e1ndula pineal que regula el sue\u00f1o y puede verse afectada por tumores en esta gl\u00e1ndula."}{"title": "RECEPTORES DE SOMATOSTATINA:Los receptores de somatostatina son prote\u00ednas que se encuentran en la superficie de las c\u00e9lulas y que median los efectos de la somatostatina."}{"title": "CLASIFICACI\u00d3N DE KNOSP:La clasificaci\u00f3n de Knosp es un sistema utilizado para evaluar la invasi\u00f3n de los tumores hipofisarios en el seno cavernoso mediante im\u00e1genes de resonancia magn\u00e9tica."}{"title": "PROTE\u00cdNA GS:La prote\u00edna GS es una prote\u00edna que puede mutar en algunos tumores hipofisarios, afectando su comportamiento y secreci\u00f3n hormonal."}{"title": "GENES AIP Y PRKAR1A:Los genes AIP y PRKAR1A est\u00e1n implicados en la patog\u00e9nesis de los adenomas hipofisarios y pueden influir en su desarrollo."}{"title": "SUBTIPOS DE RECEPTORES:Los subtipos de receptores de somatostatina, como SSTR2 y SSTR5, influyen en la respuesta tumoral a los an\u00e1logos de somatostatina."}{"title": "ACROMEGALIA:Acromegalia is a chronic hormonal disorder caused by the hypersecretion of growth hormone (GH), often due to pituitary adenomas. This condition leads to abnormal growth of bones and tissues, resulting in various clinical changes and health risks. Individuals with acromegalia may experience somatic growth, which can contribute to multiple comorbidities and an increased risk of premature mortality. The disorder can also affect sex hormone-binding globulin (SHBG) levels, further complicating the health profile of those affected. Overall, acromegalia is characterized by significant physical changes and a range of associated health challenges."}{"title": "CORTICOTROPINOMA SILENTE:El corticotropinoma silente es un tipo de adenoma hipofisario que no presenta s\u00edntomas evidentes y se clasifica en la nueva actualizaci\u00f3n de la OMS."}{"title": "ADENOMA HIPOFISARIO:Adenoma hipofisario is a benign tumor of the pituitary gland that can lead to various health issues due to its potential to produce excess hormones. This type of tumor originates in the pituitary gland and can cause significant hormonal and clinical alterations. Specifically, adenoma hipofisario may result in the overproduction of growth hormone, which can lead to conditions such as acromegaly, as well as excess adrenocorticotropic hormone (ACTH), which is associated with Cushing's syndrome. These tumors are classified based on their cellular type and hormonal characteristics, highlighting the diversity in their presentation and effects on the body."}{"title": "ADENOMA SOMATOTROPO ESCASAMENTE GRANULADO:Un tipo de adenoma hipofisario que se caracteriza por una baja granulaci\u00f3n y se ha reconocido por su agresividad cl\u00ednica."}{"title": "MACROADENOMA LACTOTROPO EN VARONES:Un adenoma hipofisario que afecta a los varones y se clasifica como macroadenoma, mostrando caracter\u00edsticas cl\u00ednicas espec\u00edficas."}{"title": "ADENOMA DE C\u00c9LULAS DE CROOKE:Un tipo de adenoma hipofisario que se clasifica en la nueva actualizaci\u00f3n de la OMS y se asocia con caracter\u00edsticas histol\u00f3gicas particulares."}{"title": "ADENOMA PLURIHORMONAL PIT-1 POSITIVO:Un adenoma hipofisario que produce m\u00faltiples hormonas y se clasifica como Pit-1 positivo, anteriormente conocido como adenoma hipofisario silente subtipo III."}{"title": "PITUICITOMAS:Tumores de bajo grado de origen glial que se originan en la hip\u00f3fisis posterior y son infrecuentes, a menudo diagnosticados en adultos."}{"title": "CRANEOPARINGIOMAS:CRANEOPARINGIOMAS son tumores que afectan la hip\u00f3fisis y se clasifican en dos grupos seg\u00fan su histolog\u00eda y alteraciones moleculares. Estos tumores son benignos y se originan de los restos de la bolsa de Rathke. Pueden causar s\u00edntomas compresivos en la infancia o adolescencia, lo que resalta su impacto en el desarrollo y la salud de los pacientes j\u00f3venes."}{"title": "QUISTE DE RATHKE:Un tipo de quiste que se forma a partir de restos de la bolsa de Rathke, que puede encontrarse en la regi\u00f3n selar."}{"title": "ANEURISMAS CAROT\u00cdDEOS:Dilataciones anormales de las arterias carot\u00eddeas que pueden afectar la regi\u00f3n selar y causar complicaciones."}{"title": "F\u00cdSTULAS CAROT\u00cdDEAS ARTERIOVENOSAS:Conexiones anormales entre las arterias y venas carot\u00eddeas que pueden tener implicaciones cl\u00ednicas en la regi\u00f3n selar."}{"title": "MASAS SELARES:Las masas selares son lesiones que pueden encontrarse en la regi\u00f3n de la silla turca, donde se localiza la gl\u00e1ndula pituitaria, e incluyen tumores, quistes y otros procesos."}{"title": "TUMORES DE C\u00c9LULAS GERMINALES:Los tumores de c\u00e9lulas germinales son neoplasias que pueden aparecer en la regi\u00f3n selar y son considerados malignos."}{"title": "CORDOMA:El cordoma es un tumor maligno que puede localizarse en la regi\u00f3n selar y se origina de restos de la notocorda."}{"title": "CARCINOMA HIPOFISARIO:El carcinoma hipofisario es un tipo de tumor maligno que afecta la gl\u00e1ndula pituitaria y es menos com\u00fan que los adenomas."}{"title": "LINFOMAS:LINFOMAS are a type of cancer characterized by malignant tumors that can metastasize to the pituitary gland, potentially affecting its function. Additionally, LINFOMAS can lead to adrenal insufficiency, highlighting their serious impact on the body's endocrine system."}{"title": "HORMONAS ADENOHIPOFISARIAS:Las hormonas adenohipofisarias son producidas por la gl\u00e1ndula pituitaria anterior y son cruciales para diversas funciones endocrinas."}{"title": "FACTORES DE TRANSCRIPCI\u00d3N HIPOFISARIOS:Los factores de transcripci\u00f3n hipofisarios son prote\u00ednas que regulan la expresi\u00f3n de genes en las c\u00e9lulas de la gl\u00e1ndula pituitaria."}{"title": "\u00cdNDICE KI67:El \u00edndice Ki67 es un marcador utilizado para evaluar la proliferaci\u00f3n celular en tumores, incluyendo adenomas hipofisarios."}{"title": "RECUENTO DE MITOSIS:El recuento de mitosis es una t\u00e9cnica utilizada para evaluar la actividad proliferativa de los tumores, incluyendo los adenomas hipofisarios."}{"title": "INVASI\u00d3N TUMORAL:La invasi\u00f3n tumoral se refiere a la capacidad de un tumor para infiltrarse en tejidos adyacentes, un aspecto importante en la evaluaci\u00f3n de la agresividad de los adenomas hipofisarios."}{"title": "MEN 1:El s\u00edndrome MEN 1 es una neoplasia endocrina m\u00faltiple que se asocia con adenomas hipofisarios y otros tumores endocrinos."}{"title": "CANCER DE MAMA:El c\u00e1ncer de mama puede dar met\u00e1stasis en la hip\u00f3fisis, afectando su funci\u00f3n."}{"title": "FGF-4:El FGF-4 es un receptor del factor de crecimiento que puede estar alterado en algunos adenomas hipofisarios."}{"title": "HIPERTENSI\u00d3N INTRACRANEAL:La hipertensi\u00f3n intracraneal puede ser un s\u00edntoma asociado a tumores en el \u00e1rea selar, como los adenomas hipofisarios."}{"title": "HORMONAS:Hormonas refers to a group of various hormones tested in patients, including insulin, glucagon, and serotonin. These hormones are chemical messengers produced by glands in the body that play a crucial role in regulating a wide array of physiological processes, such as growth, metabolism, reproduction, mood, and the body's response to stress. They are essential for coordinating activities like lipid metabolism and maintaining cardiovascular health, as well as regulating water and electrolyte balance.\n\nHormones can be significantly affected by conditions such as pituitary adenomas, which may lead to clinical alterations. Additionally, they are involved in treatments for gender affirmation, including the use of estrogen and anti-androgens. Specific hormones, such as testosterone, are vital in treating conditions like hypogonadism, while others, like estrogens and androgens, are important for bone mass regulation and can influence the risk of osteoporosis. Overall, hormones are regulatory substances that are integral to maintaining homeostasis and overall health in the body."}{"title": "COMPLEJO DE CARNEY:El complejo de Carney es un s\u00edndrome raro de endoplasia endocrina m\u00faltiple que se hereda de forma autos\u00f3mica dominante, asociado a mutaciones en el gen PRKAR1A y caracterizado por lesiones pigmentadas cut\u00e1neas y tumores mixomatosos."}{"title": "PRKAR1A:El gen PRKAR1A codifica para una subunidad reguladora de la prote\u00edna cinasa A y est\u00e1 relacionado con el complejo de Carney."}{"title": "CTNNB1:El gen CTNNB1 codifica la \u03b2-catenina y puede estar relacionado con la formaci\u00f3n de craneofaringiomas."}{"title": "BRAF:BRAF is a gene that can be associated with the formation of craniopharyngiomas through V600E mutations. This oncogene is frequently mutated in papillary craniopharyngiomas, which predominantly occur in adults."}{"title": "HYPERPLASIA HIPOFISARIA:La hiperplasia hipofisaria se define como un aumento en el volumen y contenido celular de la hip\u00f3fisis, que puede ocurrir en situaciones como el embarazo y el hipotiroidismo."}{"title": "NEVUS AZUL:El nevus azul es una lesi\u00f3n pigmentada cut\u00e1nea asociada con el complejo de Carney."}{"title": "LENTIGOS:Los lentigos son lesiones pigmentadas cut\u00e1neas que tambi\u00e9n se asocian con el complejo de Carney."}{"title": "TUMORES MIXOMATOSOS:Los tumores mixomatosos son un tipo de tumor que puede aparecer en el contexto del complejo de Carney, afectando el coraz\u00f3n, la piel o la mama."}{"title": "TUMORES DE C\u00c9LULAS DE SERTOLI:Los tumores de c\u00e9lulas de Sertoli son un tipo de tumor endocrino que puede estar relacionado con el complejo de Carney."}{"title": "TUMORES DE C\u00c9LULAS DE LEYDIG:Los tumores de c\u00e9lulas de Leydig son otro tipo de tumor endocrino que puede estar relacionado con el complejo de Carney."}{"title": "TUMORES TIROIDEOS:Los tumores tiroideos son alteraciones endocrinol\u00f3gicas que pueden asociarse con el complejo de Carney.)<|COMPLETE|>"}{"title": "CASTA\u00d1O I ET AL.:Casta\u00f1o I es un autor que ha contribuido a la investigaci\u00f3n sobre adenomas hipofisarios y sus hallazgos moleculares."}{"title": "HARSH GR ET AL.:Harsh GR es un autor que ha escrito sobre craneofaringiomas y su tratamiento en la literatura m\u00e9dica."}{"title": "HIPOFISITIS LINFOC\u00cdTICA:La hipofisitis linfoc\u00edtica es la forma m\u00e1s frecuente de hipofisitis primaria, asociada a una etiolog\u00eda autoinmunitaria y que puede causar d\u00e9ficits hormonales."}{"title": "MICROADENOMA:MICROADENOMA refers to a small tumor of the pituitary gland, typically measuring less than 1 cm. It is often associated with the production of thyroid-stimulating hormone (TSH) and is relevant in the context of thyroid hormone resistance. Microadenomas are more common in women and are frequently treated with surgical intervention."}{"title": "AULINAS A:Aulinas A es uno de los autores del Manual de Endocrinolog\u00eda y Nutrici\u00f3n que aborda la hipofisitis."}{"title": "WEBB S:Webb S es uno de los autores del Manual de Endocrinolog\u00eda y Nutrici\u00f3n que aborda la hipofisitis."}{"title": "RESMINI E:Resmini E es uno de los autores del Manual de Endocrinolog\u00eda y Nutrici\u00f3n que aborda la hipofisitis."}{"title": "CEFAL\u00c9A:La cefalea es un s\u00edntoma que puede presentarse de forma aguda en pacientes con hipofisitis, a menudo asociado con s\u00edntomas compresivos."}{"title": "HORMONAS AUTOINMUNITARIAS:Las hormonas autoinmunitarias son marcadores que pueden estar presentes en pacientes con hipofisitis, indicando un proceso autoinmunitario."}{"title": "RMN:RMN, or resonancia magn\u00e9tica nuclear (magnetic resonance imaging), is a non-invasive medical imaging technique widely utilized for diagnostic purposes. It is particularly effective in evaluating various conditions, including pituitary disorders such as hipofisitis and pituitary tumors. Additionally, RMN is relevant in the assessment of adrenal tumors, as it provides detailed images that help characterize adrenal nodules and lesions. The technique has also been employed to suggest the presence of mucinous tumors and to detect metastases in patients with medullary thyroid carcinoma. Overall, RMN serves as a crucial tool in the diagnosis and characterization of a range of medical conditions, particularly those related to the endocrine system."}{"title": "HALLAZGOS RADIOL\u00d3GICOS:Los hallazgos radiol\u00f3gicos son observaciones en im\u00e1genes que pueden ayudar a diferenciar entre hipofisitis y adenomas hipofisarios."}{"title": "ATROFIA HIPOFISARIA:La atrofia hipofisaria es una posible consecuencia evolutiva de la hipofisitis, donde el tejido normal es reemplazado por fibrosis."}{"title": "FIBROSIS:Fibrosis is a pathological process characterized by the formation of scar tissue in various organs, which can significantly impair their function. In the context of the heart, fibrosis leads to alterations that affect its performance. Additionally, fibrosis can occur in conditions such as hypophysitis, where normal tissue is replaced by fibrous tissue, further illustrating the diverse implications of this process across different bodily systems."}{"title": "PROLACTINOMA:Prolactinoma is a type of pituitary tumor that produces an excessive amount of prolactin, leading to a condition known as hyperprolactinemia. This overproduction of prolactin can result in various clinical symptoms, including hypogonadism. The management of hyperprolactinemia is a central focus in addressing the effects of prolactinoma, highlighting its significance in both diagnosis and treatment."}{"title": "GALACTORREA:Galactorrea is defined as the abnormal flow of milk from the breast, which can occur in both men and women. This condition is often associated with elevated levels of prolactin, a hormone that can be indicative of various underlying health issues, such as Multiple Endocrine Neoplasia type 1 (MEN1). In medical terms, galactorrea is linked to hyperprolactinemia, a condition characterized by excessive prolactin in the bloodstream."}{"title": "HYPERPROLACTINEMIA:Hyperprolactinemia is a medical condition characterized by elevated levels of prolactin in the blood. This condition can lead to various symptoms and health issues, including decreased libido, impotence, and infertility. Hyperprolactinemia may be caused by pituitary tumors or certain medications. The condition is recognized in both English and Spanish, with the Spanish description emphasizing the same key points regarding its causes and symptoms."}{"title": "CARCINOMA BRONCOG\u00c9NICO:El carcinoma broncog\u00e9nico es un tipo de c\u00e1ncer de pulm\u00f3n que puede producir prolactina de manera ect\u00f3pica, contribuyendo a la hiperprolactinemia."}{"title": "ANTIDEPRESIVOS:Los antidepresivos, que incluyen clases como los tric\u00edclicos y los inhibidores de la recaptaci\u00f3n de serotonina, son medicamentos utilizados para tratar la depresi\u00f3n y otros trastornos del estado de \u00e1nimo. Sin embargo, uno de los efectos secundarios asociados con su uso es la hiperprolactinemia, una condici\u00f3n caracterizada por niveles elevados de prolactina en la sangre."}{"title": "ANTIPSIC\u00d3TICOS:Los antipsic\u00f3ticos, especialmente los de primera generaci\u00f3n, son conocidos por inducir hiperprolactinemia debido a su efecto sobre la dopamina."}{"title": "AGONISTAS DOPAMIN\u00c9RGICOS:Los agonistas dopamin\u00e9rgicos son medicamentos utilizados en el tratamiento de los prolactinomas, ya que ayudan a reducir los niveles de prolactina."}{"title": "CIMETIDINA:La cimetidina es un medicamento que puede causar hiperprolactinemia como efecto secundario, afectando la secreci\u00f3n de prolactina."}{"title": "ANTICONCEPTIVOS ORALES:Anticonceptivos orales are oral contraceptives that can have complex interactions with vitamin metabolism. Their use may lead to increased plasma concentrations of ceruloplasmin and copper in the body. Additionally, anticonceptivos orales can cause elevated levels of prolactin, which may contribute to hyperprolactinemia in some women."}{"title": "HIPERPROLACTINEMIA:Hiperprolactinemia is a medical condition characterized by elevated levels of prolactin in the blood. This condition can arise from various causes, including pituitary tumors, certain medications, and other physiological conditions. It is noted that the patient's mother also has a history of hiperprolactinemia, which is associated with her health issues. Overall, hiperprolactinemia is a multifactorial condition that requires careful evaluation to determine its underlying causes and appropriate management."}{"title": "FARMACOS:Farmacos refers to drugs that are currently being tested for the treatment of obesity. Additionally, these medications are known to be a common cause of hyperprolactinemia, as they act on central aminergic pathways. Furthermore, Farmacos can also influence the outcomes of medical tests, particularly those related to blood detection in feces."}{"title": "ENFERMEDADES INFILTRATIVAS DEL HIPOT\u00c1LAMO:Las enfermedades infiltrativas del hipot\u00e1lamo, como la tuberculosis y la sarcoidosis, pueden afectar la producci\u00f3n de prolactina."}{"title": "HIPOTIROIDISMO PRIMARIO:El hipotiroidismo primario puede estar asociado con hiperprolactinemia y galactorrea."}{"title": "INSUFICIENCIA ADRENAL:Adrenal insufficiency, known as \"insuficiencia adrenal\" in Spanish, is a medical condition characterized by the inadequate production of steroid hormones by the adrenal glands. This condition can also be associated with hyperprolactinemia, which is an elevated level of prolactin in the blood."}{"title": "S\u00cdNDROME DE OVARIO POLIQU\u00cdSTICO:The S\u00edndrome de Ovario Poliqu\u00edstico, commonly known as Polycystic Ovary Syndrome (PCOS), is a hormonal disorder prevalent among women of reproductive age, affecting approximately 6-15% of this population. This condition is characterized by a range of symptoms, including irregular menstrual periods, amenorrhea (the absence of menstruation), and hyperandrogenism, which can manifest as excess hair growth. \n\nPCOS is also associated with enlarged ovaries that contain small cysts on their outer edges. It is recognized as an endocrinopathy that can lead to anovulation, which is the failure to ovulate. Additionally, the syndrome can result in hyperprolactinemia, a condition characterized by elevated levels of prolactin in the blood.\n\nFurthermore, women with PCOS are at an increased risk of developing Diabetes Mellitus Type 2, highlighting the metabolic implications of the disorder. The syndrome is often discussed in the context of various hormonal and reproductive health issues, making it a significant concern in women's health."}{"title": "TORRES VELA E:Torres Vela E is a notable author in the field of endocrinology, recognized for their contributions to medical literature. They have authored a practical guide focused on the diagnosis and treatment of acromegaly, a condition characterized by excessive growth hormone. Additionally, Torres Vela E is a contributor to the \"Manual de Endocrinolog\u00eda y Nutrici\u00f3n,\" a comprehensive resource that addresses various topics within endocrinology, including hyperprolactinemia and its treatment. Through these works, Torres Vela E has made significant strides in enhancing the understanding and management of endocrine disorders."}{"title": "LOPEZ MEZQUITA TORRES E:L\u00f3pez Mezquita Torres E is a co-author of the Manual de Endocrinolog\u00eda y Nutrici\u00f3n, focusing on endocrine disorders including hyperprolactinemia."}{"title": "CABERGOLINA:Cabergolina is a medication primarily used to treat hyperprolactinemia, a condition characterized by elevated levels of prolactin in the blood. It is particularly effective for patients with prolactinomas, which are benign tumors of the pituitary gland that produce excess prolactin. Additionally, Cabergolina functions as a dopamine agonist, which means it can stimulate dopamine receptors in the brain. This action allows it to inhibit the secretion of growth hormone, making it useful in cases where there is a mild elevation of insulin-like growth factor 1 (IGF-1). Overall, Cabergolina plays a significant role in managing hormonal imbalances related to prolactin and growth hormone levels."}{"title": "MACROPROLACTINOMA:Macroprolactinoma is a larger type of prolactinoma, which is a specific kind of pituitary tumor that produces elevated levels of prolactin. This overproduction of prolactin can result in hyperprolactinemia, a condition characterized by various hormonal imbalances and associated symptoms. Due to the significant health issues that can arise from macroprolactinomas, they may necessitate surgical intervention to manage the condition effectively."}{"title": "MICROPROLACTINOMA:Microprolactinoma is a small tumor of the pituitary gland that produces excess prolactin, which can significantly impact the patient's treatment options. It is a smaller variant of prolactinoma, a type of tumor that is more common and typically managed with medication."}{"title": "L\u00d3PEZ MEZQUITA TORRES E:L\u00f3pez Mezquita Torres E is an author of the Manual de Endocrinolog\u00eda y Nutrici\u00f3n, contributing to the field of endocrinology."}{"title": "IPILIMUMAB:Ipilimumab is a monoclonal antibody utilized in immunotherapy for the treatment of various tumors, notably melanoma and renal cell carcinoma. As an immune checkpoint inhibitor, it enhances the immune response against cancer cells. However, ipilimumab is associated with several adverse effects, the most common being hypophysitis, which can disrupt hormone levels, including prolactin. This condition may lead to secondary adrenal insufficiency due to its impact on the pituitary gland. Overall, ipilimumab plays a significant role in cancer treatment while also presenting risks of autoimmune reactions."}{"title": "VERAPAMILO:Verapamil, also known as Verapamilo, is a calcium antagonist and calcium channel blocker primarily used in the treatment of high blood pressure and angina. It is recognized for its potential side effect of causing hyperprolactinemia, which can occur in up to 8.5% of users. Additionally, Verapamil is utilized in managing symptoms associated with late dumping syndrome. Overall, it serves multiple therapeutic purposes while also being linked to elevated prolactin levels in some patients."}{"title": "LACTANCIA:LACTANCIA refers to the process of breastfeeding, which involves feeding a baby with breast milk and has specific nutritional requirements for the mother. It encompasses various aspects, including dietary reference intakes tailored for the Spanish population, particularly focusing on infants and children. The term also highlights the importance of breastfeeding for individuals aged 14-18 years, who have unique dietary recommendations.\n\nBreastfeeding is a critical concern for patients diagnosed with conditions such as microprolactinoma, as it can influence their nutritional needs and health. During the lactation period, which is when a mother produces milk for her infant, specific dietary recommendations are established for different age groups, including infants. These recommendations include defined nutrient intake levels and metrics for females under 18 years.\n\nAdditionally, lactation is evaluated for its impact on energy requirements, particularly during the first and second semesters of breastfeeding. It is important to note that lactation can be affected by certain medications, such as tiamazol and PTU, which are used to treat hyperthyroidism. Overall, LACTANCIA encompasses the multifaceted nature of breastfeeding, its nutritional implications, and the specific dietary guidelines that support both mothers and their children during this crucial period."}{"title": "HIPOFSIS:The pituitary gland, which is involved in hormone production and can be affected by tumors and medications."}{"title": "PACIENTE GESTANTE:"}{"title": "PROLACTIN:Prolactin is a hormone that plays a crucial role in stimulating milk production in mammals. Its levels can be influenced by various factors, including certain medications such as risperidone, which can lead to a condition known as hyperprolactinemia."}{"title": "RISPERIDONE:Risperidone is an antipsychotic medication that can cause elevated prolactin levels, leading to hyperprolactinemia."}{"title": "FAMILIAL HYPERPROLACTINEMIA:Familial hyperprolactinemia is a genetic condition associated with mutations that affect prolactin receptor function."}{"title": "GAUDY C:Gaudy C is one of the authors referenced in the study on ipilimumab-induced hypophysitis."}{"title": "CASTINETTI F:Castinetti F is one of the authors referenced in the study on ipilimumab-induced hypophysitis."}{"title": "CARR\u00c9 T:Carr\u00e9 T is one of the authors referenced in the study on ipilimumab-induced hypophysitis."}{"title": "MORANGE I:Morange I is one of the authors referenced in the study on ipilimumab-induced hypophysitis."}{"title": "CONTE-DEVOLX B:Conte-Devolx B is one of the authors referenced in the study on ipilimumab-induced hypophysitis."}{"title": "EUROPEAN JOURNAL OF ENDOCRINOLOGY:The European Journal of Endocrinology is a scientific journal dedicated to publishing research in the field of endocrinology. It covers a wide range of topics, including studies on thyroid carcinoma and various hormonal disorders. Notably, this journal is also the platform where significant research, such as the study on ipilimumab-induced hypophysitis, has been published, highlighting its role in disseminating important findings in endocrinological research."}{"title": "ALBAREL F:"}{"title": "UPTODATE INC:UpToDate Inc. is a comprehensive medical resource that offers evidence-based information and clinical decision support for healthcare professionals. The organization provides detailed literature reviews and treatment guidelines on a wide range of medical conditions, including hypercalcemia, pheochromocytoma, hyperprolactinemia, Cushing's syndrome, osteoporosis management, and adrenocortical carcinoma. UpToDate Inc. is recognized as a reliable source of updated medical information, serving as a reference for various health topics and conditions, including hypogonadism. The resource is designed to assist healthcare professionals in making informed clinical decisions by providing access to current medical literature and guidelines."}{"title": "VENLAFAXINA:Venlafaxina is a medication that is primarily used as an antidepressant to treat depressive disorders. It functions as a serotonin and norepinephrine reuptake inhibitor, which means it helps to increase the levels of these neurotransmitters in the brain, thereby improving mood and alleviating symptoms of depression. In some patients, venlafaxina may be associated with hyperprolactinemia, a condition characterized by elevated levels of prolactin. This medication was prescribed to the patient for managing her psychiatric condition, highlighting its role in the treatment of mental health issues."}{"title": "RISPERIDONA:Risperidona, conocida en ingl\u00e9s como risperidone, es un antipsic\u00f3tico de segunda generaci\u00f3n que se utiliza en el tratamiento de diversas condiciones psiqui\u00e1tricas. Este medicamento se asocia frecuentemente con la hiperprolactinemia, lo que implica que puede provocar aumentos significativos en los niveles de prolactina en el organismo."}{"title": "MACROPROLACTINA:La macroprolactina es una forma de prolactina que se forma por la uni\u00f3n de la mol\u00e9cula nativa de prolactina a la inmunoglobulina G, causando hiperprolactinemia anal\u00edtica."}{"title": "HYPERPROLACTINEMIA FAMILIAR:"}{"title": "BUPROPION:Bupropion is a medication that has been approved for the treatment of depression and for aiding smoking cessation. It functions as a norepinephrine and dopamine reuptake inhibitor, which means it helps to increase the levels of these neurotransmitters in the brain. Additionally, bupropion is known to influence appetite regulation and reward mechanisms. Notably, it does not appear to affect prolactin levels, making it a unique option among antidepressants."}{"title": "ANTIPSICOTICOS:Antipsychotics, known as \"antipsic\u00f3ticos\" in Spanish, are medications primarily used to treat psychiatric disorders. They are particularly noted for being the most common pharmacological cause of hyperprolactinemia, especially among first-generation antipsychotics. Additionally, some antipsychotics are associated with the development of the Syndrome of Inappropriate Antidiuretic Hormone secretion (SIADH)."}{"title": "AMISULPIRIDA:Amisulpride is another second-generation antipsychotic linked to frequent and marked increases in prolactin levels."}{"title": "SINDROME DE CUSHING:Cushing's syndrome is a condition caused by chronic exposure to high levels of cortisol, often due to a pituitary tumor producing ACTH."}{"title": "HIPOFISIS:The pituitary gland, also known as the hipofisis, is a small gland situated at the base of the brain. It plays a crucial role in the endocrine system by producing various hormones, one of which is adrenocorticotropic hormone (ACTH). The presence of tumors in the pituitary gland can lead to the overproduction of ACTH, potentially resulting in Cushing's syndrome, a condition characterized by excessive cortisol levels in the body."}{"title": "TAYLOR D:Taylor D is an author of a publication discussing antidepressant-induced hyperprolactinemia."}{"title": "VILLAR-TAIBO R:Villar-Taibo R is an author of a publication discussing prolactin disorders."}{"title": "SIFONTES-DUBON M:Sifontes-Dubon M is an author of a publication discussing prolactin disorders."}{"title": "BERNABEU-MORON I:Bernabeu-Moron I is an author of a publication discussing prolactin disorders."}{"title": "COKER F:"}{"title": "RMN HIPOFISARIA:La RMN hipofisaria es un procedimiento diagn\u00f3stico esencial que se utiliza para evaluar diversas condiciones relacionadas con la gl\u00e1ndula pituitaria. Este tipo de resonancia magn\u00e9tica es especialmente recomendado para ni\u00f1os que presentan pubertad precoz central, particularmente en aquellos menores de 9 a\u00f1os. Adem\u00e1s, la RMN hipofisaria es una t\u00e9cnica de imagen eficaz para detectar adenomas corticotropos en pacientes que tienen sospechas de enfermedad de Cushing. En resumen, la RMN hipofisaria es una herramienta clave en la evaluaci\u00f3n de trastornos endocrinos, proporcionando informaci\u00f3n valiosa para el diagn\u00f3stico y tratamiento de estas condiciones."}{"title": "TAC:TAC, or Tomograf\u00eda Axial Computarizada, is a diagnostic imaging procedure widely utilized in medical diagnostics to visualize internal structures of the body. This imaging technique, also known as computed tomography (CT), is particularly effective in identifying tumors and other abnormalities across various organs. It is commonly employed to detect lung tumors, pheochromocytomas, and adrenal nodules, among other conditions.\n\nThe TAC provides detailed images that assist in diagnosing and monitoring the progression of diseases, including the evaluation of medullary thyroid carcinoma and the assessment of lesions over time. It has been noted that while TAC is a valuable tool for detecting tumors, it may be less sensitive than magnetic resonance imaging (MRI) for certain conditions, such as corticotroph adenomas.\n\nIn specific cases, TAC has been used to confirm the dilation of the Wirsung duct and to study irregularities in the pancreatic process. Additionally, it is recommended for evaluating extensive cervical involvement in patients with medullary thyroid carcinoma. Overall, TAC is an essential imaging modality in the medical field, often used in conjunction with other imaging methods to enhance diagnostic accuracy."}{"title": "CATETERISMO DE SENOS PETROSOS:The \"CATETERISMO DE SENOS PETROSOS\" is a medical procedure employed to assess the hypersecretion of adrenocorticotropic hormone (ACTH) produced by the pituitary gland, particularly in cases where magnetic resonance imaging (MRI) fails to identify a tumor. This procedure, known as petrosal sinus sampling, is specifically utilized to measure ACTH levels, aiding in the differentiation of the source of ACTH in patients diagnosed with Cushing's syndrome."}{"title": "NIEMAN LK:Nieman LK is a prominent medical professional and author recognized for his extensive contributions to the literature on Cushing's syndrome, including its epidemiology, diagnosis, and treatment. He has authored multiple guidelines and literature reviews that address various aspects of the syndrome, including the establishment of its causes and clinical manifestations. Nieman LK is frequently cited in references related to Cushing's syndrome, highlighting his significant role in advancing the understanding and management of this condition. His work encompasses a comprehensive examination of hypercortisolism and its implications, making him a key figure in the field."}{"title": "LACROIX A:LACROIX A is an editor and author recognized in the literature concerning both the syndrome of Cushing and the treatment of adrenocortical carcinoma. This individual is cited in various references related to these medical topics, highlighting their contributions to the understanding and management of these conditions."}{"title": "KETOCONAZOL:KETOCONAZOL is a medication primarily used in the treatment of Cushing's syndrome. It functions by inhibiting the production of cortisol in the adrenal glands, effectively addressing the hormonal imbalances associated with this condition. Ketoconazole works by inhibiting several enzymes involved in steroidogenesis, which further supports its role in managing elevated cortisol levels."}{"title": "METIRAPONA:Metirapona is a medication that functions as an inhibitor of adrenal steroidogenesis, specifically targeting the enzyme 11-\u03b2-hydroxylase. This action effectively reduces cortisol production, making metirapona a valuable treatment option for individuals suffering from Cushing's syndrome."}{"title": "PASIRE\u00d3TIDA:El pasire\u00f3tida es un f\u00e1rmaco que act\u00faa directamente sobre la secreci\u00f3n de ACTH hipofisaria y se utiliza en el tratamiento del s\u00edndrome de Cushing."}{"title": "MIFEPRISTONA:Mifepristona, tambi\u00e9n conocida como mifepristone, es un antagonista de los receptores de progesterona que, en dosis elevadas, tambi\u00e9n act\u00faa como un antagonista de los receptores de glucocorticoides. Se utiliza en el tratamiento del s\u00edndrome de Cushing, una condici\u00f3n caracterizada por la sobreproducci\u00f3n de cortisol. Su capacidad para bloquear estos receptores la convierte en una opci\u00f3n terap\u00e9utica importante en el manejo de esta enfermedad."}{"title": "PASIREOTIDA:Pasireotida is a novel somatostatin analog characterized by its high affinity for multiple somatostatin receptors. It is primarily utilized in the treatment of Cushing's syndrome. The mechanism of action of Pasireotida involves its effect at the pituitary level, where it reduces the secretion of adrenocorticotropic hormone (ACTH)."}{"title": "TAC DE CUERPO ENTERO:Whole-body CT scan is a diagnostic imaging technique used to detect tumors in the body."}{"title": "RMN DE CUERPO ENTERO:Whole-body MRI is a diagnostic imaging technique that provides detailed images of the body's internal structures."}{"title": "PET:PET, or positron emission tomography, is an advanced imaging technique that is particularly sensitive for diagnosing metastases of malignant paragangliomas, making it a valuable tool in oncology. This imaging test provides insights into how tissues and organs are functioning, which is crucial for cancer diagnosis. Overall, PET is recognized for its effectiveness in detecting and assessing various types of cancer, enhancing the ability to monitor disease progression and treatment response."}{"title": "\u00c1LVAREZ SAN MART\u00cdN RM:\u00c1lvarez San Mart\u00edn RM is an author of a manual on endocrinology and nutrition."}{"title": "URIOSTE FONDO A:Urioste Fondo A is an author of a manual on endocrinology and nutrition."}{"title": "VIDAL CASARIEGO A:Vidal Casariego A is a notable contributor to the book titled 'Dietoterapia, nutrici\u00f3n cl\u00ednica y metabolismo', where he focuses on the dietary treatment of obesity. Additionally, he is the author of a manual that addresses topics related to endocrinology and nutrition, further highlighting his expertise in the fields of dietetics and clinical nutrition."}{"title": "TRATAMIENTO CON GH:El tratamiento con GH (hormona de crecimiento) es un enfoque terap\u00e9utico para la talla baja y otras condiciones relacionadas con el crecimiento."}{"title": "S\u00cdNDROME DE TURNER:El S\u00edndrome de Turner es una alteraci\u00f3n sexual cromos\u00f3mica que afecta a las mujeres, caracterizada por la p\u00e9rdida total o parcial del cromosoma X. Esta condici\u00f3n gen\u00e9tica se manifiesta con s\u00edntomas como talla baja, insuficiencia gonadal, amenorrea primaria y diversas anomal\u00edas f\u00edsicas y hormonales. La prevalencia del s\u00edndrome es de aproximadamente 1 por cada 2,000 a 2,500 reci\u00e9n nacidas vivas. Adem\u00e1s, el S\u00edndrome de Turner puede estar asociado con un mayor riesgo de desarrollar enfermedades como la enfermedad cel\u00edaca. Es importante destacar que esta condici\u00f3n puede requerir tratamiento con hormona de crecimiento (GH) para abordar algunas de sus complicaciones."}{"title": "S\u00cdNDROME DE PRADER-WILLI:Sindrome de Prader-Willi is a genetic disorder that affects growth and is also an approved indication for GH treatment."}{"title": "S\u00cdNDROME DE NOONAN:Sindrome de Noonan is a genetic disorder that can cause growth issues, but is not approved for GH treatment in Spain."}{"title": "TALLA BAJA IDIOP\u00c1TICA:Talla baja idiop\u00e1tica is a condition of short stature with no known cause, which is treated with GH in the United States but not in Spain."}{"title": "GEN SHOX:El gen SHOX est\u00e1 relacionado con el crecimiento y su alteraci\u00f3n puede causar deficiencia de crecimiento, lo que puede ser tratado con GH."}{"title": "MICRO-ADENOMAS:Micro-adenomas are small tumors of the pituitary gland that can affect hormone production, relevant in the context of Cushing's disease."}{"title": "MACRO-ADENOMAS:Macro-adenomas are larger tumors of the pituitary gland that can lead to excessive hormone production, significant in the context of Cushing's disease."}{"title": "HORMONA DE CRECIMIENTO:The \"HORMONA DE CRECIMIENTO,\" or Growth Hormone, is a hormone that plays a crucial role in stimulating growth, cell reproduction, and regeneration. It is utilized in various medical treatments, particularly for patients with growth deficiencies. In the context of critical care, growth hormone is mentioned as a potential treatment option for patients, including pediatric patients with extensive burns, to aid in their recovery. \n\nResearch indicates that growth hormone can enhance magnesium absorption in the body. Additionally, while growth hormone treatment has been shown to increase muscle mass, the results regarding strength improvements have been inconsistent across different clinical trials. Overall, growth hormone is a significant therapeutic agent in both pediatric and critical care settings, aimed at promoting recovery and addressing growth-related issues."}{"title": "ARTRALGIAS:Artralgias (Joint pain) are a common side effect associated with growth hormone treatment."}{"title": "GINECOMASTIA:Ginecomastia, also known as gynecomastia, is a medical condition characterized by the enlargement of breast tissue in males. This condition can arise due to various factors, including hormonal imbalances, and is often noted as a rare side effect of growth hormone treatment. Ginecomastia can occur in individuals with specific genetic conditions, such as Klinefelter syndrome and Wilson's disease, where hormonal imbalances are prevalent. Additionally, it can manifest during puberty as a natural developmental change. The condition may also be a side effect of testosterone therapy, leading to an increase in breast tissue. Overall, ginecomastia is a multifaceted condition that can result from a variety of hormonal influences and medical treatments."}{"title": "HIPERTENSI\u00d3N INTRACRANEAL BENIGNA:Hipertensi\u00f3n intracraneal benigna (Benign Intracranial Hypertension) is a rare side effect of growth hormone treatment that can lead to increased pressure in the skull."}{"title": "NEVUS:Nevus (Mole) refers to a pigmented skin lesion that may increase in number, size, and pigmentation as a side effect of growth hormone treatment.)<|COMPLETE|>"}{"title": "PEIN\u00d3 R.:Pein\u00f3 R. is the author of the \"Manual de Endocrinolog\u00eda y Nutrici\u00f3n,\" a comprehensive work that addresses growth hormone deficiency and its treatment. The manual covers this condition in both children and adults, providing valuable insights into its implications and management across different age groups."}{"title": "GH RECOMBINANTE:GH recombinante refers to the recombinant growth hormone used in medical treatments, which can have various side effects."}{"title": "DEFICIT DE GH:Deficit de GH refers to growth hormone deficiency, a medical condition that impacts growth and development in both children and adults. This condition is significant in the context of treatment and evaluation, as it can lead to various health issues if not addressed."}{"title": "TALLA BAJA:Talla Baja is a condition characterized by short stature, defined as height significantly below the average for a child's age and sex. This condition can occur as a long-term consequence in patients with Glycogen Storage Disease Type 0 (GSD0). Additionally, Talla Baja can manifest in patients with Mitochondrial Encephalomyopathy, Lactic Acidosis, and Stroke-like episodes (MELAS) due to hormonal deficiencies. Overall, Talla Baja encompasses various underlying causes and is an important consideration in the assessment of growth and development in affected individuals."}{"title": "SOMATOTROPINA HUMANA RECOMBINANTE:Somatotropina humana recombinante is a synthetic form of human growth hormone used in medical treatments for growth hormone deficiency."}{"title": "ANOMAL\u00cdAS ESTRUCTURALES:Anomal\u00edas estructurales refer to structural anomalies that can accompany severe growth hormone deficiency in children."}{"title": "DENSIDAD \u00d3SEA:Densidad \u00f3sea refers to the measure of bone strength and health, specifically indicating the amount of mineral content within a given volume of bone. This measurement can be influenced by various factors, including growth hormone levels. Techniques such as quantitative computed tomography are commonly used to evaluate densidad \u00f3sea, providing insights into the overall condition of the bones."}{"title": "MASA MAGRA:Masa Magra refers to lean body mass, which is a critical factor in evaluating nutritional status and health outcomes in chronic diseases. It encompasses the amount of muscle and tissue in the body, and this composition can be influenced by various factors, including growth hormone treatment. Understanding Masa Magra is essential for assessing overall health and managing chronic conditions effectively."}{"title": "VELOCIDAD DE CRECIMIENTO:Velocidad de crecimiento is a measure of how quickly a child grows, which is important for assessing growth hormone deficiency."}{"title": "TALLA MEDIA PARENTAL:Talla media parental is a reference height based on the average height of parents, used in assessing children's growth."}{"title": "DEFINICI\u00d3N DE CRITERIOS AUXOL\u00d3GICOS:Definici\u00f3n de criterios auxol\u00f3gicos refers to the established guidelines for assessing growth and diagnosing growth disorders."}{"title": "S\u00cdNDROME DE INTERRUPCI\u00d3N DEL TALLA HIPOFISARIO:El s\u00edndrome de interrupci\u00f3n del tallo hipofisario es una condici\u00f3n que afecta la funci\u00f3n de la hip\u00f3fisis, a menudo resultando en deficiencias hormonales."}{"title": "INFARTO HIPOFISARIO:El infarto hipofisario es una condici\u00f3n m\u00e9dica que implica la muerte del tejido hipofisario, lo que puede resultar en deficiencias hormonales."}{"title": "HEMOCROMATOSIS HEREDITARIA:Hemochromatosis hereditaria is a genetic condition characterized by excessive iron absorption and accumulation in the body. This disorder can lead to various complications, including diabetes, which is commonly observed in symptomatic patients. Additionally, hereditary hemochromatosis may result in iron deposits in the pituitary gland, potentially affecting its function."}{"title": "TUMORES NASOFAR\u00cdNGEOS:Los tumores nasofar\u00edngeos son crecimientos anormales en la nasofaringe que pueden afectar la hip\u00f3fisis y causar deficiencias hormonales."}{"title": "TRAUMA CRANEAL:El trauma craneal puede da\u00f1ar la hip\u00f3fisis, resultando en problemas hormonales como el hipopituitarismo."}{"title": "TUMORES CEREBRALES:TUMORES CEREBRALES, or brain tumors, can significantly impact various bodily functions, including swallowing and digestion. This impairment may necessitate the use of enteral nutrition to ensure that affected individuals receive adequate nourishment."}{"title": "PEGVISOMANT:Pegvisomant is a growth hormone receptor antagonist used in the treatment of acromegaly, preventing the action of growth hormone but not its secretion."}{"title": "KATZNELSON L:Katznelson L is a prominent researcher and author recognized for his significant contributions to the understanding and treatment of acromegaly. He has played a vital role in developing clinical practice guidelines for the management of this condition, further establishing his expertise in the field."}{"title": "AN\u00c1LOGOS DE SOMATOSTATINA:Somatostatin analogs are medications that inhibit the secretion of growth hormone and are used in the treatment of acromegaly."}{"title": "CORDIDO F ET AL.:Cordido F et al. authored a practical guide for the diagnosis and treatment of acromegaly published in Endocrinol Nutr in 2013."}{"title": "SOCIETY ESPA\u00d1OLA DE ENDOCRINOLOG\u00cdA Y NUTRICI\u00d3N:The Sociedad Espa\u00f1ola de Endocrinolog\u00eda y Nutrici\u00f3n is a prominent Spanish society dedicated to the fields of endocrinology and nutrition. This professional organization plays a crucial role in providing guidelines and recommendations for the management of various conditions, including diabetes and acromegaly. In 2005, the society published a monograph that outlined evidence-based nutritional recommendations, further emphasizing its commitment to advancing knowledge in these areas. Overall, the Sociedad Espa\u00f1ola de Endocrinolog\u00eda y Nutrici\u00f3n focuses on the study and treatment of endocrine disorders, contributing significantly to the healthcare landscape in Spain."}{"title": "HO PJ ET AL.:Ho PJ et al. conducted research on the regulation of pulsatile growth hormone secretion in normal subjects and patients with acromegaly."}{"title": "KATZNELSON L ET AL.:Katznelson L et al. provided clinical practice guidelines for acromegaly published in J Clin Endocrinol Metab in 2014."}{"title": "X-LAG:X-linked acrogigantism syndrome (X-LAG) is a condition characterized by early-onset gigantism due to genetic mutations."}{"title": "ADENOMA HIPOFISARIO SOMATOTROPO:"}{"title": "CARDIOVASCULAR DISEASE:Cardiovascular disease refers to a group of disorders affecting the heart and blood vessels. This condition encompasses a range of ailments that can be influenced by various factors, particularly dietary and lifestyle choices. Key dietary factors linked to cardiovascular disease include fat and sodium intake, as well as fiber and omega-3 fatty acids. Additionally, obesity and diabetes are significant risk factors associated with the prevalence of cardiovascular disease.\n\nThe condition can be exacerbated by testosterone treatment and is often discussed in relation to metabolic health. It is also noted that cardiovascular disease is associated with increased mortality in patients with acromegaly. Preventative measures for cardiovascular disease can include dietary modifications, such as adopting low-fat diets like the Ornish and Pritikin diets.\n\nOverall, cardiovascular disease is a complex health issue that is influenced by a combination of dietary habits, lifestyle factors, and underlying health conditions, making it a critical area of study and intervention in public health."}{"title": "HORMONAL DISORDERS:Hormonal disorders refer to conditions that result from an imbalance in hormone levels, which can lead to various health issues, including acromegaly."}{"title": "MUTACIONES ACTIVANTES:Activating mutations are genetic changes that lead to increased activity of certain proteins, such as those involved in hormone production, and are often implicated in conditions like acromegaly."}{"title": "HIPERPLASIA:Hyperplasia refers to the increase in the number of cells in an organ or tissue, which can lead to overproduction of hormones, including growth hormone in the context of acromegaly."}{"title": "S\u00cdNDROME DE MCCUNE-ALBRIGHT:McCune-Albright syndrome is a genetic disorder characterized by fibrous dysplasia of bone, skin pigmentation, and precocious puberty, often associated with hormonal imbalances."}{"title": "MACROADENOMAS:"}{"title": "MELMED S.:Melmed S. is a prominent researcher and author recognized for his significant contributions to the understanding of acromegaly, including its causes and clinical manifestations. He is notably an author and editor of the Williams Textbook of Endocrinology, which serves as a key reference in the field of endocrinology. Through his work, Melmed S. has made substantial contributions to academic literature, enhancing the knowledge and understanding of endocrine disorders."}{"title": "KATZNELSON L.:Katznelson L. is a researcher and author who has contributed to the understanding of acromegaly and its treatment."}{"title": "ACROMEGALY:Acromegaly is a hormonal disorder that results from excess growth hormone, leading to enlarged bones and tissues."}{"title": "TRANSSEFENOIDAL SURGERY:Transsphenoidal surgery is a common treatment option for acromegaly, particularly for microadenomas."}{"title": "TUMORS:Tumors, such as microadenomas and macroadenomas, are often involved in the development of acromegaly."}{"title": "SURGICAL TREATMENT:Surgical treatment is a common approach for managing acromegaly, particularly for tumor removal."}{"title": "HYPERINSULINISM:Hyperinsulinism is a metabolic condition characterized by excessive levels of insulin in the body. This condition often leads to hypoglycemia, which is a dangerously low level of glucose in the blood. Hyperinsulinism can be associated with insulinoma, a type of tumor that produces excess insulin. Additionally, it can arise due to the effects of excess growth hormone, further complicating the metabolic balance."}{"title": "HYPERTIGLYCERIDEMIA:Hypertriglyceridemia is a metabolic condition characterized by elevated levels of triglycerides in the blood. This condition often necessitates management, particularly in patients receiving nutritional support. Additionally, hypertriglyceridemia can be associated with acromegaly, indicating a potential link between these two health issues."}{"title": "HYPERCALCIURIA:Hypercalciuria is a medical condition characterized by the presence of excessive calcium in the urine. This condition is often studied in relation to the formation of kidney stones, as the elevated levels of calcium can contribute to their development. Additionally, hypercalciuria may occur in patients with acromegaly, a disorder resulting from excess growth hormone, which can lead to various metabolic changes affecting calcium levels."}{"title": "HYPERPHOSPHATEMIA:Hyperphosphatemia is a medical condition characterized by elevated levels of phosphate in the blood. This condition can occur in various populations, including preterm infants, and is often discussed in the context of dietary phosphorus management, particularly in patients with chronic kidney disease. Additionally, hyperphosphatemia can be associated with metabolic imbalances linked to excess growth hormone levels. Overall, it is important to monitor and manage phosphate levels to prevent potential complications related to this condition."}{"title": "HORMONAL DISORDER:"}{"title": "CASTA\u00d1O I:Casta\u00f1o I is an author of a study on the clinical impact of molecular findings in pituitary adenomas."}{"title": "MART\u00cdNEZ DE LA PISCINA I:Mart\u00ednez de la Piscina I is an author of a study on the clinical impact of molecular findings in pituitary adenomas."}{"title": "PORTILLO N:Portillo N is an author of a study on the clinical impact of molecular findings in pituitary adenomas."}{"title": "RICA I:Rica I is an author of a study on the clinical impact of molecular findings in pituitary adenomas."}{"title": "CORDIDO F:Cordido F is an author of a practical guide on the diagnosis and treatment of acromegaly."}{"title": "GARC\u00cdA ARN\u00c9S JA:Garc\u00eda Arn\u00e9s JA is an author of a practical guide on the diagnosis and treatment of acromegaly."}{"title": "MARAZUELA ASPIROZ M:Marazuela Aspiroz M is an author of a practical guide on the diagnosis and treatment of acromegaly."}{"title": "LAWS ER JR:Laws ER Jr is an author of clinical practice guidelines for acromegaly."}{"title": "MURAD MH:Murad MH is a multifaceted professional engaged in various aspects of medical research and clinical practice. He is notably involved in the development of clinical practice guidelines for pheochromocytoma and paraganglioma, as well as acromegaly. Additionally, Murad MH has contributed to the Endocrine Society Clinical Practice Guideline concerning the endocrine treatment of gender-dysphoric individuals, demonstrating his commitment to advancing care in this area.\n\nIn the realm of obesity research, Murad MH has conducted systematic reviews of obesity treatments and has studied the effects of pharmacological interventions for obesity. His work reflects a dedication to improving treatment options and outcomes for patients dealing with obesity and related endocrine disorders. Overall, Murad MH's contributions span both clinical guidelines and research, highlighting his significant role in the field of endocrinology."}{"title": "UTZ A:Utz A is an author of clinical practice guidelines for acromegaly."}{"title": "WASS JA:Wass JA is an author of clinical practice guidelines for acromegaly."}å1␀␀␀␀␀∑å1␀␀␀␀␀‘ç1␀␀␀␀␀cé1␀␀␀␀␀è1␀␀␀␀␀æê1␀␀␀␀␀Më1␀␀␀␀␀—ë1␀␀␀␀␀tí1␀␀␀␀␀¬ì1␀␀␀␀␀1î1␀␀␀␀␀¬î1␀␀␀␀␀öï1␀␀␀␀␀˛ñ1␀␀␀␀␀Öó1␀␀␀␀␀ò1␀␀␀␀␀ùò1␀␀␀␀␀Üö1␀␀␀␀␀ßö1␀␀␀␀␀Tõ1␀␀␀␀␀Íõ1␀␀␀␀␀ ú1␀␀␀␀␀vù1␀␀␀␀␀°1␀␀␀␀␀≥°1␀␀␀␀␀R¢1␀␀␀␀␀w¢1␀␀␀␀␀ë¢1␀␀␀␀␀∫¢1␀␀␀␀␀7ß1␀␀␀␀␀R®1␀␀␀␀␀∆®1␀␀␀␀␀9©1␀␀␀␀␀æ©1␀␀␀␀␀¸™1␀␀␀␀␀£´1␀␀␀␀␀L¨1␀␀␀␀␀À¨1␀␀␀␀␀KÆ1␀␀␀␀␀Ë∞1␀␀␀␀␀¢±1␀␀␀␀␀í≥1␀␀␀␀␀E¥1␀␀␀␀␀p∂1␀␀␀␀␀)∑1␀␀␀␀␀‘∑1␀␀␀␀␀pπ1␀␀␀␀␀˜∫1␀␀␀␀␀ÿª1␀␀␀␀␀iº1␀␀␀␀␀ıº1␀␀␀␀␀Yæ1␀␀␀␀␀¯æ1␀␀␀␀␀Y¡1␀␀␀␀␀¬1␀␀␀␀␀∑¬1␀␀␀␀␀B√1␀␀␀␀␀ƒ1␀␀␀␀␀¿ƒ1␀␀␀␀␀·ƒ1␀␀␀␀␀x≈1␀␀␀␀␀'∆1␀␀␀␀␀ù∆1␀␀␀␀␀Y…1␀␀␀␀␀ı…1␀␀␀␀␀w 1␀␀␀␀␀®Õ1␀␀␀␀␀,Œ1␀␀␀␀␀®Œ1␀␀␀␀␀*œ1␀␀␀␀␀ÿœ1␀␀␀␀␀ü—1␀␀␀␀␀G“1␀␀␀␀␀¿“1␀␀␀␀␀=”1␀␀␀␀␀√”1␀␀␀␀␀M‘1␀␀␀␀␀º‘1␀␀␀␀␀ÿ‘1␀␀␀␀␀Ü’1␀␀␀␀␀ ÷1␀␀␀␀␀[◊1␀␀␀␀␀—◊1␀␀␀␀␀]ÿ1␀␀␀␀␀”ÿ1␀␀␀␀␀VŸ1␀␀␀␀␀˘Ÿ1␀␀␀␀␀x⁄1␀␀␀␀␀1‹1␀␀␀␀␀Ω‹1␀␀␀␀␀F›1␀␀␀␀␀Ó›1␀␀␀␀␀gﬁ1␀␀␀␀␀Ôﬁ1␀␀␀␀␀äﬂ1␀␀␀␀␀‡1␀␀␀␀␀—‡1␀␀␀␀␀i·1␀␀␀␀␀≥‰1␀␀␀␀␀CÂ1␀␀␀␀␀␀Ê1␀␀␀␀␀áÊ1␀␀␀␀␀Á1␀␀␀␀␀πÁ1␀␀␀␀␀‘Á1␀␀␀␀␀`Ë1␀␀␀␀␀ÂË1␀␀␀␀␀tÈ1␀␀␀␀␀ïÈ1␀␀␀␀␀§Î1␀␀␀␀␀VÏ1␀␀␀␀␀”Ï1␀␀␀␀␀uÒ1␀␀␀␀␀{Û1␀␀␀␀␀Ù1␀␀␀␀␀v˙1␀␀␀␀␀T¸1␀␀␀␀␀d˛1␀␀␀␀␀Î˛1␀␀␀␀␀Ì␀2␀␀␀␀␀û2␀␀␀␀␀‹2␀␀␀␀␀ä2␀␀␀␀␀‹
